{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1562938-archmagic-levels","id":1562938,"title":"Archmagic Levels","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Mage: The Ascension"],"posts":[{"date":"2026-08-10T04:06:57-07:00","id":1562938,"title":"Archmagic Levels","content":"So, I guess we can all agree that nobody here is very found of the &quot;Masters of the Arts&quot;, right?<br /> <br /> Good, so here now is my solution to the problem of &quot;Archmastery&quot;.<br /> <br /> First, forget the dots up to 10 or 9, this is not Vampire the Masquerade.<br /> <br /> Level 6 Spheres define &quot;Arch-master&quot;. That's it, that's the pinnacle. Any more than that (theoretical level 7) and you become an Examplar instead, a lobotomized part of the &quot;hive-mind&quot; embodiment of the concept of the Sphere rather than a free willed agent. For instance, at &quot;Entropy 7&quot; you're no longer a powerful Magus, you are Fate itself, and you have no more agency at all, you're a mere manifestation of Destiny.<br /> <br /> So, with that out of the way, let us look at each one of the monstrosities I've created for each lvl 6, I think you guys might enjoy these so, let's see... I'll start with LIFE, please tell me what you think<br /> <br /> (By the way, there's a few interactions with some other Spheres, sometimes even some other lvl 6 spheres, don't worry, I'll explain each one in due time)<br /> <br /> And yes, ChatGPT helped. It helped, not made it all out, but helped me flesh some of the ideas I already had<br /> <br /> <b>LIFE 6 \u2014 REDEFINE THE BIOLOGICAL PARADIGM</b><br /> <br /> <b>Core principle</b><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"><b>Life 6 allows an Archmaster to redefine the fundamental biological principles by which living organisms exist, develop, reproduce, evolve, and interact with their environments.</b></div> <br /> Life 5 can create <b>new life</b>.<br /> <br /> Life 6 can establish <b>new rules for what life itself can be</b>.<br /> <br /> That distinction is crucial.<br /> <br /> A Life 5 Archmaster can say:<div style=\"margin-left:40px\"><i>\u201cI shall create a new species.\u201d</i></div> <br /> A Life 6 Archmaster can say:<div style=\"margin-left:40px\"><b>\u201cI shall establish a new biological paradigm under which this species\u2014and potentially all life\u2014operates.\u201d</b></div> <br /> It isn't simply <i>more</i> biological complexity.<br /> <br /> It's <b>a qualitative change in biological possibility</b>. <hr /> <b>1. The basic examples</b><br /> <br /> <br /> Let's begin with relatively mundane applications. <b>\ud83e\udec0 \u201cLife Does Not Age\u201d</b><br /> <br /> <br /> The Archmaster establishes that biological aging is no longer an intrinsic consequence of cellular existence.<br /> <br /> A population can still:<ul><li>suffer injuries;</li> <li>become infected;</li> <li>starve;</li> <li>die from trauma;</li> <li>eventually die from other causes.</li> </ul><br /> But <b>age itself no longer causes biological deterioration</b>.<br /> <br /> That's Life 6.<br /> <br /> Not:<div style=\"margin-left:40px\">\u201cI heal this person every time they age.\u201d</div> <br /> Instead:<div style=\"margin-left:40px\"><b>\u201cAging is no longer part of the biological paradigm.\u201d</b></div> <hr /> <b>\ud83e\uddec \u201cRegeneration Is Normal\u201d</b><br /> <br /> <br /> The Archmaster establishes:<div style=\"margin-left:40px\"><b>\u201cLiving tissue naturally reconstructs itself toward its proper biological pattern.\u201d</b></div> <br /> A creature doesn't possess a magical healing factor.<br /> <br /> Its biology simply works according to a different rule.<br /> <br /> A severed limb isn't magically restored.<br /> <br /> <b>Regeneration is simply what its cells do.</b><br /> <br /> This is particularly useful for distinguishing Life 5 from Life 6.<br /> <br /> A Life 5 Mage can create an organism that regenerates.<br /> <br /> Life 6 can establish <b>regeneration as a fundamental biological principle</b>. <hr /> <b>2. Redefining reproduction</b><br /> <br /> <br /> This is where Life 6 becomes much more interesting.<br /> <br /> Suppose an Archmaster establishes:<div style=\"margin-left:40px\"><b>\u201cBiological reproduction no longer requires two parents.\u201d</b></div> <br /> A species could reproduce through:<ul><li>budding;</li> <li>parthenogenesis;</li> <li>cellular division;</li> <li>environmental triggers;</li> <li>deliberate genetic recombination;</li> <li>even acquiring characteristics from unrelated organisms.</li> </ul><br /> Again, Life 5 could create a species that does any of those things.<br /> <br /> Life 6 allows the Archmaster to establish <b>a fundamentally new reproductive principle</b>. <hr /> <b>3. The Xenomorph problem</b><br /> <br /> <br /> Our earlier example becomes particularly useful here.<br /> <br /> Suppose you want something resembling the Xenomorphs from <i>Alien</i>.<br /> <br /> A Life 5 Archmaster can potentially create the species itself:<div style=\"margin-left:40px\"><b>A completely novel, viable, hereditary lifeform.</b></div> <br /> But suppose you want the following principle:<div style=\"margin-left:40px\"><b>\u201cThe developmental biology of this organism incorporates the biological characteristics of its host.\u201d</b></div> <br /> Now we're approaching Life 6 territory.<br /> <br /> The Archmaster isn't merely making an organism that has a weird reproductive cycle.<br /> <br /> They have established a <b>new biological rule for heredity and development</b>:<div style=\"margin-left:40px\"><b>A living organism can incorporate another organism's biological pattern into its own developmental program.</b></div> <br /> You could therefore have a species whose offspring aren't simply genetically inherited from their parents.<br /> <br /> Their development is partly determined by <b>the organism that hosted their development</b>.<br /> <br /> That's qualitatively stranger. <hr /> <b>4. The really important distinction: species vs paradigm</b><br /> <br /> <br /> This is probably the single most important thing to preserve. <b>Life 5</b><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"><b>Create the Vulcans.</b></div><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"><b>Create Elves.</b></div><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"><b>Create Xenomorphs.</b></div><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"><b>Create a completely novel species capable of reproducing itself.</b></div> <br /> All potentially Life 5.<br /> <br /> But Life 6 might say:<div style=\"margin-left:40px\"><b>\u201cAll vertebrate organisms can now incorporate acquired biological characteristics into their hereditary material.\u201d</b></div> <br /> Now you've changed <b>biology itself</b>.<br /> <br /> The Archmaster hasn't created a species.<br /> <br /> They have altered the <b>rules under which species exist</b>. <hr /> <b>5. \u201cWhat if I want magical organisms?\u201d</b><br /> <br /> <br /> Here's where our previous discussion becomes important.<br /> <br /> Life 6 <b>doesn't automatically become \u201cLife 5 + magic bullshit.\u201d</b><br /> <br /> Suppose you want:<div style=\"margin-left:40px\"><b>A living star.</b></div> <br /> That's not automatically Life 6.<br /> <br /> If it's literally an organism made of energy, you'd probably need:<br /> <br /> <b>Life + Forces</b><br /> <br /> and potentially:<br /> <br /> <b>Prime</b><br /> <br /> depending on what makes it supernatural.<br /> <br /> Similarly:<div style=\"margin-left:40px\"><b>A telepathic frog species</b></div> <br /> might involve:<br /> <br /> <b>Life + Mind</b><br /> <br /> rather than being a Life 6 effect merely because telepathy is exotic.<br /> <br /> And:<div style=\"margin-left:40px\"><b>A spirit that reproduces biologically</b></div> <br /> could require:<br /> <br /> <b>Life + Spirit.</b><br /> <br /> This keeps Life 6 from becoming an omnipotence button.<br /> <br /> Life 6 determines <b>the biological rules</b>.<br /> <br /> Other Spheres determine what <i>other ontological categories</i> biology is allowed to incorporate. <hr /> <b>6. A genuinely Life-6 creature</b><br /> <br /> <br /> Here's where we can make something that <i>doesn't</i> simply look like an exotic animal.<br /> <br /> Suppose the Archmaster establishes:<div style=\"margin-left:40px\"><b>\u201cAn organism's biological pattern is not determined exclusively by its physical genetic material.\u201d</b></div> <br /> Instead, its biological identity is determined by:<br /> <br /> <b>genetics + environment + memory + developmental history.</b><br /> <br /> Now two genetically identical organisms could become biologically different organisms simply because they experienced different environments.<br /> <br /> That's not merely epigenetics exaggerated to absurdity.<br /> <br /> The Archmaster has changed what <b>constitutes biological inheritance</b>.<br /> <br /> That's Life 6. <hr /> <b>7. \u201cEvolution can happen deliberately\u201d</b><br /> <br /> <br /> Another fun one:<div style=\"margin-left:40px\"><b>\u201cWhenever an organism encounters a persistent environmental challenge, its descendants automatically develop adaptations appropriate to that challenge.\u201d</b></div> <br /> Not natural selection.<br /> <br /> Not accelerated mutation.<br /> <br /> The biological paradigm itself says:<div style=\"margin-left:40px\"><b>Life responds to environmental pressures by intentionally incorporating appropriate adaptations into its hereditary pattern.</b></div> <br /> A population exposed to extreme cold eventually produces descendants biologically adapted to extreme cold.<br /> <br /> A population living in darkness eventually develops functional alternatives to vision.<br /> <br /> A population exposed to an entirely new toxin eventually produces descendants inherently immune to it.<br /> <br /> That's not merely \u201cfast evolution.\u201d<br /> <br /> You've changed <b>how evolution works</b>. <hr /> <b>8. \u201cLife defines its own phenotype\u201d</b><br /> <br /> <br /> We could push it further.<br /> <br /> Suppose Life 6 establishes:<div style=\"margin-left:40px\"><b>\u201cAn organism's biological pattern is determined by its conception of itself.\u201d</b></div> <br /> Now the creature's body develops according to its own internal biological self-model.<br /> <br /> A creature that believes itself capable of flight develops the anatomical structures necessary for flight.<br /> <br /> A species that collectively develops a new biological identity gradually changes its physiology accordingly.<br /> <br /> This is getting extremely weird\u2014but notice that it's still recognizably <b>Life</b>.<br /> <br /> We're changing the <b>rules governing biological form</b>. <hr /> <b>9. A very important permutation: Life 6 + Mind</b><br /> <br /> <br /> This is where things get <i>really</i> fun.<br /> <br /> Suppose:<br /> <br /> <b>Life 6:</b><div style=\"margin-left:40px\">Biological phenotype is determined partly by mental state.</div> <br /> <b>Mind:</b><div style=\"margin-left:40px\">Manipulate the mental state.</div> <br /> Now you could potentially create organisms whose bodies <b>respond directly to thought</b>.<br /> <br /> A sufficiently advanced combination could produce something like:<div style=\"margin-left:40px\"><i>\u201cThink of yourself as aquatic \u2192 your body becomes physiologically aquatic.\u201d</i></div> <br /> Or:<div style=\"margin-left:40px\"><i>\u201cA population believes itself to possess a particular biological trait \u2192 successive generations actually acquire it.\u201d</i></div> <br /> That's an excellent example of <b>Sphere synergy</b>.<br /> <br /> Neither Sphere alone is doing everything.<br /> <br /> Life establishes the biological rule.<br /> <br /> Mind manipulates the cognitive variable involved in that rule. <hr /> <b>10. Life 6 + Spirit</b><br /> <br /> <br /> Now connect it to our Spirit 6 discussion.<br /> <br /> Suppose:<br /> <br /> <b>Spirit 6:</b><div style=\"margin-left:40px\">Spiritual entities can exist in a previously incompatible ontological relationship with physical organisms.</div> <br /> <b>Life 6:</b><div style=\"margin-left:40px\">Living organisms can incorporate spiritual entities into their biological existence.</div> <br /> Now you could potentially create:<div style=\"margin-left:40px\"><b>A genuinely biological species whose organisms possess spirits as intrinsic biological components.</b></div> <br /> Not:<div style=\"margin-left:40px\">\u201cA normal animal with a ghost attached.\u201d</div> <br /> The organism's biological paradigm itself includes a spiritual component.<br /> <br /> This becomes especially relevant to our <b>vampire + Avatar</b> example.<br /> <br /> Spirit 6 establishes:<div style=\"margin-left:40px\"><b>Vampiric existence and Avatar existence can coexist.</b></div> <br /> Life 6 could potentially go further and redefine the biological/undead paradigm so that:<div style=\"margin-left:40px\"><b>The spiritual component is an intrinsic, inheritable component of the organism's biological identity.</b></div> <br /> That starts becoming something very close to a completely new category of living existence. <hr /> <b>11. Life 6 + Prime 6</b><br /> <br /> <br /> And now we can do the really ridiculous one. \ud83d\ude02<br /> <br /> Prime 6 says:<div style=\"margin-left:40px\"><b>A magical mechanism can become an intrinsic and objective component of reality.</b></div> <br /> Life 6 says:<div style=\"margin-left:40px\"><b>Biological existence can operate according to a fundamentally different biological paradigm.</b></div> <br /> Combine them:<div style=\"margin-left:40px\"><b>Magic can become an intrinsic biological process.</b></div> <br /> Not an enchanted organism.<br /> <br /> Not an organism with Quintessence temporarily injected into it.<br /> <br /> Rather:<div style=\"margin-left:40px\"><b>Magic becomes metabolism.</b></div> <br /> The organism might literally:<ul><li>produce Quintessence biologically;</li> <li>consume Quintessence as nourishment;</li> <li>reproduce magical properties;</li> <li>transmit magical traits hereditarily;</li> <li>regenerate through an intrinsically magical biological mechanism.</li> </ul><br /> This is exactly where our earlier \u201csupernatural new species\u201d question ends up.<br /> <br /> <b>Life 5</b> creates the species.<br /> <br /> <b>Life 6 + Prime 6</b> can potentially make <b>magic itself part of its biology.</b> <hr /> <b>12. Life 6 + Forces 6</b><br /> <br /> <br /> Now revisit our \u201cliving star.\u201d<br /> <br /> Life 6 establishes:<div style=\"margin-left:40px\"><b>A biological organism can maintain itself without conventional biochemical metabolism.</b></div> <br /> Forces 6 establishes:<div style=\"margin-left:40px\"><b>Energy behaves according to a newly defined physical paradigm.</b></div> <br /> Together, you could potentially establish:<div style=\"margin-left:40px\"><b>An organism whose metabolism consists entirely of stellar radiation and whose physical structure is maintained through energy rather than conventional matter.</b></div> <br /> And if you want the thing to actually be <b>made of energy</b>, then Forces becomes essential.<br /> <br /> Life alone shouldn't get to sneak into Forces' territory. <hr /> <b>13. Life 6 + Matter 6</b><br /> <br /> <br /> This gets even stranger.<br /> <br /> Suppose Matter 6 allows matter to have fundamentally impossible properties.<br /> <br /> Life 6 establishes:<div style=\"margin-left:40px\"><b>Living organisms can incorporate such matter into their biological identity.</b></div> <br /> Now you might make an organism whose biological tissues are:<ul><li>perfectly indestructible;</li> <li>perfectly elastic;</li> <li>permanently crystalline;</li> <li>capable of changing phase without losing biological integrity;</li> <li>composed of a substance that ordinarily cannot exist.</li> </ul><br /> Again:<br /> <br /> <b>Life determines that it's alive.</b><br /> <br /> <b>Matter determines what its physical substance can be.</b> <hr /> <b>14. Life 6 + Correspondence 6</b><br /> <br /> <br /> Here's one of my favorites.<br /> <br /> Suppose Correspondence 6 establishes a world in which spatial locality itself has been fundamentally altered.<br /> <br /> Life 6 could then establish organisms whose biological identity <b>doesn't depend upon conventional spatial localization</b>.<br /> <br /> Imagine:<div style=\"margin-left:40px\"><b>A single organism whose body can naturally exist across multiple locations.</b></div> <br /> Not teleportation.<br /> <br /> Not duplication.<br /> <br /> Not several organisms connected by a magical link.<br /> <br /> There is <b>one biological organism</b>, and its biological Pattern simply isn't localized to one conventional spatial position.<br /> <br /> That's an excellent example of why the sixth dots can become terrifying when combined. <hr /> <b>15. Life 6 + Time 6</b><br /> <br /> <br /> Likewise:<div style=\"margin-left:40px\"><b>A species whose biological existence is not temporally localized.</b></div> <br /> An organism could potentially have a biological pattern distributed across multiple temporal states.<br /> <br /> But we should be cautious here.<br /> <br /> If you say:<div style=\"margin-left:40px\">\u201cThe organism exists simultaneously at birth, adulthood and death,\u201d</div> <br /> that's primarily a <b>Time</b> problem.<br /> <br /> Life 6's contribution would be:<div style=\"margin-left:40px\"><b>\u201cBiological identity does not require a single continuous developmental history.\u201d</b></div> <br /> Time provides the temporal mechanics.<br /> <br /> Life provides the biological paradigm that can survive them. <hr /> <b>16. Some Life 6 rotes</b><br /> <br /> <br /> Let's give the Archmaster some actual buttons to press. <b><b>The Deathless Organism</b></b><br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Life 6</b><div style=\"margin-left:40px\">Redefines biological aging so that maturation occurs normally but senescence is no longer an intrinsic biological process.</div> <br /> The target can still be killed.<br /> <br /> It simply doesn't <b>die of being old</b>. <hr /> <b><b>The Adaptive Genome</b></b><br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Life 6</b><div style=\"margin-left:40px\">Establishes a hereditary system in which organisms automatically incorporate environmentally advantageous adaptations into subsequent generations.</div> <br /> A species exposed to a new environment gradually becomes biologically adapted to it without conventional mutation and selection. <hr /> <b><b>The Ouroboros Organism</b></b><br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Life 6</b><div style=\"margin-left:40px\">Establishes a closed biological cycle in which the organism's metabolic waste becomes the raw material for its own continued metabolism.</div> <br /> It doesn't violate conservation of energy\u2014so no Forces 6 is required.<br /> <br /> The Archmaster has simply redefined <b>the biological pathway through which matter and energy circulate</b>. <hr /> <b><b>The Self-Defining Flesh</b></b><br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Life 6 + Mind</b><div style=\"margin-left:40px\">Establishes a biological paradigm in which conscious self-conception directly determines phenotype.</div> <br /> The Mind component supplies the mental variable; Life defines the mechanism by which that variable becomes biological reality. <hr /> <b><b>The Thaumobiological Species</b></b><br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Life 6 + Prime 6</b><div style=\"margin-left:40px\">Establishes a species for which magical energy is an intrinsic component of metabolism and heredity.</div> <br /> The organism doesn't <i>cast a spell to heal itself.</i><br /> <br /> Its biological system <b>is itself magical.</b> <hr /> <b><b>The Avatar-Bearing Vampire</b></b><br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Spirit 6 + Life 6 + Prime 6</b><br /> <br /> This is our earlier monstrosity. \ud83d\ude02<ul><li><b>Spirit 6:</b> Vampiric existence and Avatar existence are no longer intrinsically incompatible.</li> <li><b>Life 6:</b> The resulting condition can be incorporated into the organism's fundamental biological/undead paradigm.</li> <li><b>Prime 6:</b> Vampiric supernatural power and Awakened magic become compatible magical mechanisms.</li> </ul><br /> The result isn't merely:<div style=\"margin-left:40px\"><b>\u201cA vampire who happens to know Life 3.\u201d</b></div> <br /> It's potentially an entirely new supernatural category. <hr /> <b>17. What Life 6 emphatically does NOT mean</b><br /> <br /> <br /> This is important enough to make explicit. <b>\u274c \u201cI can make anything alive.\u201d</b><br /> <br /> <br /> Not automatically.<br /> <br /> Giving a chair consciousness might involve <b>Mind</b>.<br /> <br /> Giving it a spirit might involve <b>Spirit</b>.<br /> <br /> Giving it biological existence requires <b>Life</b>\u2014but the details matter. <b>\u274c \u201cI can create magic creatures.\u201d</b><br /> <br /> <br /> Not by Life alone. <b>\u274c \u201cI can manipulate souls.\u201d</b><br /> <br /> <br /> Not simply because souls are associated with living beings. <b>\u274c \u201cI can alter physical constants.\u201d</b><br /> <br /> <br /> That's <b>Forces</b>, Matter, Time, etc. <b>\u274c \u201cI can make anything I imagine biological.\u201d</b><br /> <br /> <br /> No.<br /> <br /> The Archmaster is redefining <b>biological possibility</b>, not gaining unrestricted reality manipulation. <hr /> <b>The final distinction</b><br /> <br /> <br /> I think this is the cleanest formulation we've arrived at: <div class=\"b-bbcode__table--wrapper text_table_\"><table class=\"b-bbcode__table text_table\"><tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"></tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"><td class=\"text_table_td\"><b>Life 1</b></td> <td class=\"text_table_td\"><b>Perceive</b> life</td> </tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"><td class=\"text_table_td\"><b>Life 2</b></td> <td class=\"text_table_td\"><b>Restore / Heal</b> and make minor changes to simple life; minor modifications to complex life</td> </tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"><td class=\"text_table_td\"><b>Life 3</b></td> <td class=\"text_table_td\"><b>Majorly modify</b> simple life; minor modifications to complex life</td> </tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"><td class=\"text_table_td\"><b>Life 4</b></td> <td class=\"text_table_td\"><b>Majorly modify</b> complex life</td> </tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"><td class=\"text_table_td\"><b>Life 5</b></td> <td class=\"text_table_td\"><b>Create fundamentally novel lifeforms/species</b></td> </tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"><td class=\"text_table_td\"><b>Life 6</b></td> <td class=\"text_table_td\"><b>Redefine the biological principles by which life itself operates</b></td> </tr> </table></div> And this gives us a very satisfying progression:<div style=\"margin-left:40px\"><b>Life 1 \u2014 Know life.</b><br /> <b>Life 2 \u2014 Repair life.</b><br /> <b>Life 3 \u2014 Reshape life.</b><br /> <b>Life 4 \u2014 Fundamentally redesign complex life.</b><br /> <b>Life 5 \u2014 Create new life.</b><br /> <b>Life 6 \u2014 Redefine what life can be.</b></div> <br /> That last distinction is the one I'd protect most fiercely as we revise the remaining Spheres.<br /> <br /> And importantly, <b>Life 6 doesn't make Life 5 obsolete</b>. Life 5 is still the level at which you can sit down and say <i>\u201cI want to make a completely new species with these characteristics\u201d</i>. Life 6 instead allows you to change the <b>rules that make those characteristics biologically possible in the first place</b>.<br /> <br /> That's our revised <b>Life 6</b>.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4e","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/29126-phooku","name":"Phooku","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":1,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2026"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-08-10T04:13:45-07:00","id":1562941,"title":"","content":"So, with Life 6 you can create something like the Zerg Swarm, which are organisms that don't operate under Darwinist Evolution, but rather unde Lamarckian Evolution - aka heredity is not &quot;genetics&quot;, but rather &quot;phenotypical&quot;. Meaning, someone that practice body building will have children being born already highly muscular and some such.<br /> <br /> Or it can also be like the Kroot from Warhammer 40k, which can absorb the biological characteristics of any beings that they eat - and then their descendants can inherent those characteristics.<br /> <br /> So, I'll wait for a bit before posting other Spheres","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/29126-phooku","name":"Phooku","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":1,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2026"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-08-10T07:20:12-07:00","id":1562950,"title":"","content":"So I like the idea of this escalation, though I have two places I think it may run aground.<br /> <br /> The first is how to expand it into the other Spheres, because at least one Sphere, Matter, incorporates this level of advancement into rank 5. &quot;With Mastery, the crafter can <i>create substances that transcend the limitations of scientific possibility</i>, <i>conjure materials unknown to Earthly reality...</i>&quot; You will run into problems redefining the nature of matter outside that. Not only that, but because this element is in Matter 5, there's at least some indication it should be in Life and Forces 5 as well.<br /> <br /> The second one is that I think you are muddying the waters in your examples. You often start by saying that Life can establish something new, but then in your examples you don't list anything new so your examples sound like something earlier ranks can handle.<br /> <br /> Lets use section 2 as an example. Reproduction. You list budding, parthenogenesis, and cellular division, but these are already known methods of reproduction and firmly in the earlier ranks. What you really want for examples are forms of reproduction that sound biologically unfeasible or even impossible such as:<ul><li>Reproduction by infectious screaming</li> <li>Reproduction by viral infection (as in the entire infected creatures becomes a new non-viral creature)</li> <li>Reproduction by radio waves (positive interference of light waves leads to the creation of a physical cellular entity)</li> <li>Reproduction by perception (every time a new observer sees a creature, a new copy is made)</li> </ul>I'd say the sections I noticed this in on first pass are 2, 5, 8, 9, 10, 11, 12, 13, 14, and I think there are some others that would also have issues, but I'd have to look it up. For instance, I think there already are creatures that don't have a form of senescence, but I'd have to check if that's true in a technical sense. But quite a few of your examples are things that can be done with lesser ranks. Perhaps not on the scale you envision, but certainly in the idea.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage: The Ice-ension: An Epic Game of Reality on the Rink","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/758-ramnesis","name":"Ramnesis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar758_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2220"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-08-10T08:02:39-07:00","id":1562953,"title":"","content":"I'm sorry but I would have to advice against using ChatGPT - it makes it overly long, hard to read, and it disguises it's mistakes with overly positive language that makes one thinks it knows what's talking about. If you have to use it, do a resume with fewer core points. What you want to do with Life 6 it's more understandable by your last post than the entirety of the first one.<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>1</b>.<br /> Life 5 can make you biologically ageless already, just as it can do a lot of the things listed (regeneration, changing how a creature gives birth). Chat doesnt seem to understand that Life 5 already can alter how life works at a fundamental, and supernatural, level<br /> <br /> Or was the intention that celular life doesn't age &quot;anymore, anywhere&quot;?, then you're altering how AoEs work in a similar way as how Forces 9 does it on MotA.<br /> <br /> Which of the two is it? - by the rote on 16 it seems the former was the intention, but reading the section on &quot;species vs. paradigm&quot; suggests the latter.<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>2.</b><br /> Inheritance of this trait it's where it starts getting interesting to me, tho that's more a problem with the <i>targeting</i> system of Mage than a problem of Life 5 not being able to alter how &quot;biology itself&quot; works. It's because your magickaly created new biology would have to &quot;jump&quot; to an uncountable number of targets if you want it to inherit (MotA Life 7 does cover this, it changes the way targeting works so you can create these sort of effects, among others, with countable successes)<br /> <br /> *<b>Nitpick</b>: Vampires require Matter, and Avatars are mysterious things that are Spirit and/or Prime, the reason why the Curse doesn't work well for them isn't under Life domain at all but I'm guestimating Chat just extrapolated it's Life 6 to Spirit and disregarded that Avatars are &quot;shards of Prime&quot;, and all the &quot;unknowns&quot; about the Curse and Avatars to say something Chat tought people wanted to hear.<br /> <br /> I would say there's 0 reasons to require Life for this one, you're not changing a fact about &quot;vampiric life&quot;, you're changing how the &quot;Curse of Caine&quot; work - which arguably requires Prime 6 more than anything else (since that's how it's broken in the two books where it's done).<br /> <br /> <b>In summary:</b> Chat it's ebbing back and forth from doing things Life 5 can already do (agelesness, regeneration, etc.), and thinking about Life 6 as if it was doing a scale redefinition of biology a lo Forces 9 (species vs. paradigm) + Life 6, 7 and 8 to the fold. Adding some mistakes and confusing stuff to the mixture <hr /><br /> The problem of how magick inherites it's properties it's an interesting one. Like, how do you create a generational curse (very common on myth), or how do you create a supernatural <i>species</i>?<br /> <br /> Nowhere it says that Life 5 can't alter how one reproduces at a genetical-inheritance level. But some ST could say that if you want your created magical property (such as your Zerg Lamarckian Evolution) to inherit, then you would have to increase the number of targets. As if it wasn't a biological property but an artifact that superseedes biology.<br /> <br /> The interesting thing your Life 6 it's adding it's to transform Life 5 alterations to life itself from &quot;an artifact that superseedes biology&quot; to &quot;it's how it's biology works now&quot;<br /> <br /> One could argue that's not really so much a problem of the limits of the Sphere as a problem of the limits of the <i>targeting </i>system in general. But it's not a bad idea for Life 6, after all, Life does reproduce itself.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1683,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","user":"Aleph","date":".  clarification 08-10-2026, 11:13 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","name":"Aleph","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3056"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-08-10T08:21:46-07:00","id":1562954,"title":"","content":"I'd go further, because even new forms of reproduction could just be the addition of other Spheres to the effect.<br /> <br /> The concept itself seems legit, but it's actually self defeating. To change what fundamentally defines Life you're actually running afoul of one of a few situations:<br /> <br /> 1. You're changing properties that are currently unknown, but conceptually possible and covered by previous levels. Senescence is an example, though there are organisms without it, but it wouldn't be out of place at Life 3/4.<br /> <br /> 2. You're changing a convention that's arbitrary, little more than the above writ large. There are many ways to define life in the academy, but it's a matter of semantics rather than concept incompatibility. The game accepts Life without a regular metabolism, like a virion.<br /> <br /> 3. You're bypassing other Spheres even if you don't notice it. If not Life 3+, then senescence is Entropy. Metabolism is Matter and Forces, and so on. Making a Spirit Pattern and a Life Pattern being related is just level 5, maybe with Prime added.<br /> <br /> 4. Worst case scenario, you're doing what you explicitly forbade and redefining the Sphere itself, declaring if a phenomenon should or not be covered.<br /> <br /> I think the best approach here, that is what you are trying to hit in a roundabout way, is rewrite the Magic system's rules themselves.<br /> <br /> What's really changing isn't if something can be done, but rather:<br /> <br /> - Making it Lasting, not Permanent duration.<br /> <br /> - Protecting against Disbelief and Unmaking.<br /> <br /> - Direct control to define Pattern.<br /> <br /> - Achieving Great Work with fewer successes.<br /> <br /> - Rejecting a Reality Zone.<br /> <br /> - Taking down the last hardwired limitations.<br /> <br /> My suggestion: tackle those directly. Rather than focus on conceptual explanations, Mages have a hard time even explaining such a level because it's actually defined in game terms as operationalizations over the usual rules. It csn also include passive effects, like Diff reduction for other levels.<br /> <br /> Let's write down what the rules say on how Magic works, and how Archmastery can mess with basic definitions.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-08-10T08:33:52-07:00","id":1562955,"title":"","content":"On using AI, it's really tricky.<br /> <br /> It's important to directly instruct it to criticize, to challenge assumptions and force alternative perspectives on the chat, among others. It's an interesting tool, but not an intuitive one as it is built to add confidence to whatever is said.<br /> <br /> Also choose the AI accordingly. This is not the type of work where ChatGPT shines among its peers. Claude and DeepSeek are way better at the kind of inference involved in game rules like those. Given the need for strict instructions I'd say this is firmly a work for DeepSeek. You can get Claude and Gemini to work around it, but ChatGPT was a plainly bad choice.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4e","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-08-10T08:38:00-07:00","id":1562956,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">My suggestion: tackle those directly. Rather than focus on conceptual explanations, Mages have a hard time even explaining such a level because it's actually defined in game terms as operationalizations over the usual rules. It csn also include passive effects, like Diff reduction for other levels.<br /> <br /> Let's write down what the rules say on how Magic works, and how Archmastery can mess with basic definitions.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, one common idea about Archmagick it's to alter how magick works on Arete levels 6+ instead of adding Spheres.<br /> <br /> Sphere level 5 covers almost everything imaginable, when I start thinking about exceptions, I note most are about scale and scope, and how magick itself works, not so much the concept itself being absent (and when it is, it's often a fictional concept from another game that wasn't contemplated, not because it's on a &quot;level beyond&quot;). But Arete sits there, very empty (does almost nothing beyond 5-6, unless you're a Technomancer then you can start ... to not use the tech that was your whole concept :P ), and it's very general about magick.<br /> <br /> One cound add things like &quot;inheritance&quot; or &quot;infectious&quot; as properties magick can have at high Arete levels.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1683,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","user":"Aleph","date":".  syntax correction 08-10-2026, 11:42 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","name":"Aleph","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3056"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-08-10T08:45:13-07:00","id":1562957,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1562938-archmagic-levels?p=1562954#post1562954\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> - Making it Lasting, not Permanent duration.<br /> <br /> - Protecting against Disbelief and Unmaking.<br /> <br /> - Direct control to define Pattern.<br /> <br /> - Achieving Great Work with fewer successes.<br /> <br /> - Rejecting a Reality Zone.<br /> <br /> - Taking down the last hardwired limitations.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>Arguably Lasting is a Rank 5 power. That is my best take as to what Life 5 and Mind 5 mean when they reference permanent effects. That or those spheres are arbitrarily restricted on duration unless using Rank 5.<br /> <br /> It would be interesting if Archmastery was resistant to Disbelief. Another way of putting it might be that Archmastery could make Mythic Threads or their Technocratic variants (Cosmological Constants, I think they were called). That would accomplish several of the things on that list.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage: The Ice-ension: An Epic Game of Reality on the Rink","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/758-ramnesis","name":"Ramnesis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar758_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2220"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-08-10T09:51:50-07:00","id":1562965,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aleph</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1562938-archmagic-levels?p=1562956#post1562956\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">But Arete sits there, very empty (does almost nothing beyond 5-6, unless you're a Technomancer then you can start ... to not use the tech that was your whole concept :P ), and it's very general about magick.</div> </div> </div> </div>Given its cost, already, I wouldn't be against Arete giving some benefits by itself above 5 rather than requiring extra Sphere dots, maybe at least as new Backgrounds rather than rank of Sphere, like what DtF does with Earthbound.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ramnesis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1562938-archmagic-levels?p=1562957#post1562957\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It would be interesting if Archmastery was resistant to Disbelief. Another way of putting it might be that Archmastery could make Mythic Threads or their Technocratic variants (Cosmological Constants, I think they were called). That would accomplish several of the things on that list.</div> </div> </div> </div>Cosmological Constants was the Revised term. Works as Union slang, I guess.<br /> <br /> I think it's conceptually defensible, but myself I would break it into minor aspects for finer control. Maybe a new Effects chart with how to add or take things from another level and how it changes successes required or Difficulty.<br /> <br /> And of course, at this point changing the Curse, or more generally being able to redefine or build a Major Splat could be within reach.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-08-10T12:59:13-07:00","id":1562974,"title":"","content":"So.... to the OP:<br /> <br /> 1) It's a bit bold to claim that we all dislike MotA even if most Mage fans are highly critical of how it handled Archmastery<br /> <br /> 2) While the mods don't outright ban everything &quot;AI,&quot; we are expected to post human content - including our own - and not use LLMs or generative image/video models for the content of our posts here.<br /> <br /> 3) While I think MotA's approach has issues, one of the appeals of more than one dot for Archmastery is breaking things up. Look how long your post for Life 6 alone is. If that's what it takes to define and explain one Sphere's Archmastery, it's not really a functional approach to something meant to be used in games.<br /> <br /> ----------------------<br /> <br /> More broadly speaking, a big problem with every approach to Archmastery in Mage so far (including many fan attempts I've seen) run into a big problem: there's no clear idea of what the point of Archmasters are besides mages that just do more than other mages. They don't have a unique role in the setting or narrative that isn't equally filled by high Arete mages with lots of high rankings in normal Spheres.<br /> <br /> Why should Archmagees exist as a mechanical element of the game needs to be addressed before you can start to figure out how to implement something.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-08-10T15:12:15-07:00","id":1562980,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ramnesis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1562938-archmagic-levels?p=1562950#post1562950\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So I like the idea of this escalation, though I have two places I think it may run aground.<br /> <br /> The first is how to expand it into the other Spheres, because at least one Sphere, Matter, incorporates this level of advancement into rank 5. &quot;With Mastery, the crafter can <i>create substances that transcend the limitations of scientific possibility</i>, <i>conjure materials unknown to Earthly reality...</i>&quot; You will run into problems redefining the nature of matter outside that. Not only that, but because this element is in Matter 5, there's at least some indication it should be in Life and Forces 5 as well.<br /> <br /> The second one is that I think you are muddying the waters in your examples. You often start by saying that Life can establish something new, but then in your examples you don't list anything new so your examples sound like something earlier ranks can handle.<br /> <br /> Lets use section 2 as an example. Reproduction. You list budding, parthenogenesis, and cellular division, but these are already known methods of reproduction and firmly in the earlier ranks. What you really want for examples are forms of reproduction that sound biologically unfeasible or even impossible such as:<ul><li>Reproduction by infectious screaming</li> <li>Reproduction by viral infection (as in the entire infected creatures becomes a new non-viral creature)</li> <li>Reproduction by radio waves (positive interference of light waves leads to the creation of a physical cellular entity)</li> <li>Reproduction by perception (every time a new observer sees a creature, a new copy is made)</li> </ul>I'd say the sections I noticed this in on first pass are 2, 5, 8, 9, 10, 11, 12, 13, 14, and I think there are some others that would also have issues, but I'd have to look it up. For instance, I think there already are creatures that don't have a form of senescence, but I'd have to check if that's true in a technical sense. But quite a few of your examples are things that can be done with lesser ranks. Perhaps not on the scale you envision, but certainly in the idea.</div> </div> </div> </div>Ah, I had problem with Matter, but I believe I've come up with an elegant solution to it. Maybe we should do Matter next then? I promise the idea for Matter is super cool... Actually, I believe I've come up with something cool for all spheres.<br /> <br /> I'll also confess that I became sort of lazy and just copied and pasted whatever shit the dumb AI posted, after several back and forth interactions because I was tired and didn't want the moment to pass.<br /> <br /> I guess I'll also try to reduce the size of it too, too many unnecessary information.<br /> <br /> But yeah, those are good points. The thing, the common theme that I ended up coming up with, is that the level 6 of Spheres should change the theme of the Spheres on an ontological level - basically changing the rules of what even define the thing that they represent. So, Life 6 deals with something like &quot;what even defines what are the parameters of Life, what's the ontology of Life&quot;.<br /> <br /> You'll see this same theme throughout the other lvl 6 Spheres","signature":"","edited":{"userid":29126,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/29126-phooku","user":"Phooku","date":". 08-10-2026, 06:29 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4e","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/29126-phooku","name":"Phooku","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":1,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2026"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-08-10T15:32:41-07:00","id":1562984,"title":"","content":"Why the hell can't I use more quotes?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/29126-phooku","name":"Phooku","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":1,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2026"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-08-10T15:54:44-07:00","id":1562986,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aleph</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1562938-archmagic-levels?p=1562953#post1562953\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm sorry but I would have to advice against using ChatGPT - it makes it overly long, hard to read, and it disguises it's mistakes with overly positive language that makes one thinks it knows what's talking about. If you have to use it, do a resume with fewer core points. What you want to do with Life 6 it's more understandable by your last post than the entirety of the first one.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah thats what we get for being lazy, I was already too tired to make a final edition of the content, but I'll promise I'll do for the other Spheres<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <b>1</b>.<br /> Life 5 can make you biologically ageless already, just as it can do a lot of the things listed (regeneration, changing how a creature gives birth). Chat doesnt seem to understand that Life 5 already can alter how life works at a fundamental, and supernatural, level<br /> <br /> Or was the intention that celular life doesn't age &quot;anymore, anywhere&quot;?, then you're altering how AoEs work in a similar way as how Forces 9 does it on MotA. </div> </div> </div>Life 5 can make SOMEONE ageless, as in, an individual.<br /> <br /> Life 6 would be used to make you, your children, your grandchildren, your grandchildren's children, all immortal...<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <b>2.</b><br /> Inheritance of this trait it's where it starts getting interesting to me, tho that's more a problem with the <i>targeting</i> system of Mage than a problem of Life 5 not being able to alter how &quot;biology itself&quot; works. It's because your magickaly created new biology would have to &quot;jump&quot; to an uncountable number of targets if you want it to inherit (MotA Life 7 does cover this, it changes the way targeting works so you can create these sort of effects, among others, with countable successes) </div> </div> </div>Yeah, but only when you think about a &quot;target&quot; as an individual, instead of a concept itself. It does get a bit abstract at this level... Which I think is absolutely the point.<br /> <br /> I personally do NOT put heredity at lvl 6, I instead let it go on lvls 4 and 5; I also change Life 2 to just simply be HEALING, instead of the utterly idiotic and nonsensical difference between &quot;Life 2 heals self, Life 3 heals others&quot;, which again, it is one of the many utterly idiotic, nonsensical, stupid, detestably irrational things on the official structure of the spheres, but I wanted to keep according to the official canon.<br /> <br /> The main thing about Life 6 isn't therefore precisely about solely &quot;they reproduce&quot;, but rather about changing how Life Patterns operate at a fundamental level. So for example, like Ramnesis said, having beings that reproduce no longer by sex but rather by very fantastic means, such as by sound waves (probably combining at least Forces 1 to the effect), or creating organisms that reproduce by... Let's call it sex, but instead of having only 2 sexes, you have 5... Or 17, or whatever how many other than 2 that you'd like, and you'd need at least one member of each one of your 17 &quot;sexes&quot; for successful reproduction... Things like that.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> *<b>Nitpick</b>: Vampires require Matter, and Avatars are mysterious things that are Spirit and/or Prime, the reason why the Curse doesn't work well for them isn't under Life domain at all but I'm guestimating Chat just extrapolated it's Life 6 to Spirit and disregarded that Avatars are &quot;shards of Prime&quot;, and all the &quot;unknowns&quot; about the Curse and Avatars to say something Chat tought people wanted to hear.<br /> <br /> I would say there's 0 reasons to require Life for this one, you're not changing a fact about &quot;vampiric life&quot;, you're changing how the &quot;Curse of Caine&quot; work - which arguably requires Prime 6 more than anything else (since that's how it's broken in the two books where it's done). </div> </div> </div>The Machine-God got a bit overly excited about our small chat over Vampires and end up speaking out of turn... And I was, as I said, guilty on the crime of laziness. Chat also kinda ruined my small cherry on top for when discussing Spirit 6, but there is a good reason to discuss Vampires with Spirit 6, it will go well when it happens I promise. But yeah, nothing to do with Life 6.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <b>In summary:</b> Chat it's ebbing back and forth from doing things Life 5 can already do (agelesness, regeneration, etc.), and thinking about Life 6 as if it was doing a scale redefinition of biology a lo Forces 9 (species vs. paradigm) + Life 6, 7 and 8 to the fold. Adding some mistakes and confusing stuff to the mixture <hr /><br /> The problem of how magick inherites it's properties it's an interesting one. Like, how do you create a generational curse (very common on myth), or how do you create a supernatural <i>species</i>?<br /> <br /> Nowhere it says that Life 5 can't alter how one reproduces at a genetical-inheritance level. But some ST could say that if you want your created magical property (such as your Zerg Lamarckian Evolution) to inherit, then you would have to increase the number of targets. As if it wasn't a biological property but an artifact that superseedes biology.<br /> <br /> The interesting thing your Life 6 it's adding it's to transform Life 5 alterations to life itself from &quot;an artifact that superseedes biology&quot; to &quot;it's how it's biology works now&quot;<br /> <br /> One could argue that's not really so much a problem of the limits of the Sphere as a problem of the limits of the <i>targeting </i>system in general. But it's not a bad idea for Life 6, after all, Life does reproduce itself. </div> </div> </div>The common theme I adopted for these levels is, indeed &quot;how does X thing works at a fundamental level?&quot;<br /> <br /> Maybe then I can put Matter here, to quench Ramnesis curiosity, and also to show that principle applied; I think I'll go with Mind too, which also exemplifies it well","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4e","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/29126-phooku","name":"Phooku","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":1,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2026"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-08-10T16:16:48-07:00","id":1562988,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1562938-archmagic-levels?p=1562974#post1562974\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So.... to the OP:<br /> <br /> 1) It's a bit bold to claim that we all dislike MotA even if most Mage fans are highly critical of how it handled Archmastery</div> </div> </div> </div>Nah it's not, we all hate it. Be honest, you hate it too.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> 2) While the mods don't outright ban everything &quot;AI,&quot; we are expected to post human content - including our own - and not use LLMs or generative image/video models for the content of our posts here. </div> </div> </div>I'm sorry, I didn't know you were the fashion police for the format of what people post.<br /> <br /> I use the AI to expand my ideas, sometimes work out some more examples I hadn't initially thought, and also to organize the ideas I put out, but these were ALL my ideas, I didn't just come to ChatGPT and said &quot;create lvl 6&quot; and then copy and pasted it all.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> 3) While I think MotA's approach has issues, one of the appeals of more than one dot for Archmastery is breaking things up. Look how long your post for Life 6 alone is. If that's what it takes to define and explain one Sphere's Archmastery, it's not really a functional approach to something meant to be used in games. </div> </div> </div>There are no &quot;appeals&quot; to it, it's just utterly idiotic, stupid random nonsense. And no, it's not to &quot;break things up&quot;, but rather just to reassemble Vampire the Masquerade and their equally stupid, nonsensical and completely random system of having cool powers with a shitton of black circles attached to it, that's it. And just like in Vampire, it has no sensible, logical progression to it - nor could it have, because it's just stupid.<br /> <br /> The problem I was trying to solve is that an extra level should solve the problem of being a qualitative superior layer of complexity, on a metaphysical level, of what the Sphere can do, instead of just merely &quot;more, more, MORE!&quot; which is the prevalent &quot;philosophy&quot; (if &quot;stupidity&quot; became &quot;philosophy&quot;, that is) that plagues good old White Wolf.<br /> <br /> The post is long because I was lazy to edit, or even to ask &quot;ok, make a resume of that instead&quot;. In truth, what Life 6 does is &quot;Change the Ontology of Life&quot;, everything else other than that are just examples, which can be near infinite most of the time for any Spheres at any levels.<br /> <br /> So, in a short version, what you could do it:<br /> <br /> Change the ways Life reproduce - sometimes necessitating other Spheres - such as reproducing by though, sound, maybe even weirder ways, such as adding Entropy to make a lifeform that always automatically reproduces when there's a Republican president in the USA and things of the sort.<br /> <br /> It's changing how Evolution works - no longer mutations and natural selection and some such, but rather now it's fully Lamarckian, maybe even &quot;Essence consumption&quot; such as the Zerg.<br /> <br /> So, to sum it all up, it's changing the fundamentals of how life itself operates.<br /> <br /> ----------------------<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> More broadly speaking, a big problem with every approach to Archmastery in Mage so far (including many fan attempts I've seen) run into a big problem: there's no clear idea of what the point of Archmasters are besides mages that just do more than other mages. They don't have a unique role in the setting or narrative that isn't equally filled by high Arete mages with lots of high rankings in normal Spheres.<br /> <br /> Why should Archmagees exist as a mechanical element of the game needs to be addressed before you can start to figure out how to implement something. </div> </div> </div>Why should Masters exist?<br /> <br /> That's a kind of a silly question, we could then likewise say &quot;ok, so why do we need level 5 of the Spheres?&quot;<br /> <br /> &quot;What have the Masters ever done for us?&quot;<br /> <br /> Maybe you'll change your mind thou with a few other of the lvl 6 spheres I thought out... Particularly Prime 6, because in the way I envision Prime 6, it would allow for things as &quot;Industrial Magi-Tech&quot;. As in, mass producing &quot;magic&quot;.<br /> <br /> If you're getting where I'm going with it, then you might already get that, Prime 6 then would go with &quot;change the very Ontology of Magic itself&quot;. I'll expand it more once I discuss it, but then it your question is &quot;what are Archmages role in the setting&quot;, then I would attribute one of the things - the mass production of the Techno magic Mojo of the Technocracy to them. But like I said, I'll explain more once I get into Prime<br /> <br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4e","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/29126-phooku","name":"Phooku","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":1,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2026"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-08-10T16:38:42-07:00","id":1562989,"title":"","content":"TL; DR:<br /> <br /> 1. Don't copy AI. Link if you want, but no copy.<br /> <br /> 2. The game is ontological by default.<br /> <br /> 3. All this stuff is solidly Life 5.<br /> <br /> 4. Only limitations are Mythic Threads, and for thematic reasons.<br /> <br /> 5. What we can improve are Disbelief, ease of attaining Lasting effects and scaling.<br /> <br /> 6. <i><b><span style=\"font-size:14px\">Main</span> <span style=\"font-size:14px\">question</span>: <span style=\"font-size:14px\">what</span> <span style=\"font-size:14px\">do</span> <span style=\"font-size:14px\">we</span> <span style=\"font-size:14px\">get</span> <span style=\"font-size:14px\">out</span> <span style=\"font-size:14px\">of</span> <span style=\"font-size:14px\">this?</span></b></i><br /> <br /> 7. Sphere level may be the wrong approach.<br /> <hr /><br /> I have to agree with <u><b>Heavy Arms</b></u>. I'm mostly in board with using AI as a brainstorming phase tool, if not the only one, but copying the AI and calling it a day is kind of a dick move.<br /> <br /> My suggestion in such moments is that you write a briefing and link the AI chat, that's at least more honest, then you hammer things down later.<br /> <br /> Ontological changes here are meaningless, the AI likes the word &quot;ontological&quot; and misses that the game deals with ontology by default all the time. A Pattern is basically an &quot;ontology unit&quot;, Paradigms are ontological conceptualizations of Magic, and the great tension of the game is how to reach true knowledge if your presence overrides ontological facts. <br /> <br /> The game already cover all limits of possibility at rank 5 making stuff that violate fundamental rules, even before that, revising all examples I see no reason they shouldn't be possible at 5.<br /> <br /> <u><b>Ramnesis</b></u> already touched the simplest way to describe the actual remaining limitations: the Mythic Threads, things that are arbitrarily out of reach for game reasons.<br /> <br /> And with <u><b>Aleph</b></u>'s contributions my point stand simplified: what's left to do is just to mess with Disbelief and clearer and simpler rules to make it Lasting, plus better scaling. Most examples are just that.<br /> <br /> What's really missing is the last question Heavy Arms asked: what does it accomplish for the game? Not how they're more powerful, but why to have them? What you want those Archmages to add to the story?<br /> <br /> To be blunt, my only idea for now is making for Splat Originators, which I'm quite unsure if it is a useful goal. Or Mages capable of rewriting over the Consensus in a definitive way, totally superseding it, which I also fear may be just a bad idea.<br /> <br /> Better scaling, clearer ways to make it Lasting and resistance to Disbelief may be worthy additions to the game, but not necessarily as a superior Sphere level. Either as rules revisions or new Backgrounds that require Arete 6+.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-08-10T16:41:22-07:00","id":1562990,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1562938-archmagic-levels?p=1562954#post1562954\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'd go further, because even new forms of reproduction could just be the addition of other Spheres to the effect.<br /> <br /> The concept itself seems legit, but it's actually self defeating. To change what fundamentally defines Life you're actually running afoul of one of a few situations:<br /> <br /> 1. You're changing properties that are currently unknown, but conceptually possible and covered by previous levels. Senescence is an example, though there are organisms without it, but it wouldn't be out of place at Life 3/4.<br /> <br /> 2. You're changing a convention that's arbitrary, little more than the above writ large. There are many ways to define life in the academy, but it's a matter of semantics rather than concept incompatibility. The game accepts Life without a regular metabolism, like a virion.<br /> <br /> 3. You're bypassing other Spheres even if you don't notice it. If not Life 3+, then senescence is Entropy. Metabolism is Matter and Forces, and so on. Making a Spirit Pattern and a Life Pattern being related is just level 5, maybe with Prime added.<br /> <br /> 4. Worst case scenario, you're doing what you explicitly forbade and redefining the Sphere itself, declaring if a phenomenon should or not be covered.</div> </div> </div> </div>To be fair thou, none of the nonsense came from me, but from Chatty doing Chatty things. I'm guilty of laziness thou... Which I admit, it is kind of unforgivable, but my time is usually short so please forgive me for that.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I think the best approach here, that is what you are trying to hit in a roundabout way, is rewrite the Magic system's rules themselves. </div> </div> </div>I'm trying actively NOT to have to do that, the thing I expressly do NOT want to do is &quot;ok, this is done at X Sphere on lvl 5, but I (randomly) think that this is too powerful so it should go to lvl 6'.<br /> <br /> No, my intent is to firmly have EVERYTHING that can be expressly be within the confines of any one Spheres to be firmly within the confines of the levels 1 to 5, and with QUALITATIVE INCREMENTS between levels, rather than QUANTITATIVE IMPROVEMENTS (and here I should throw my evil eye towards at least Forces Sphere and it's moronic &quot;wind, more wind, HOLY SHIT A TORNADO&quot; stupid approach, but that's another conversation), while leaving the lvl 6 towards something that goes BEYOND that, something that at a fundamental level kinda rearranges what the concept of anyone single Sphere even means. That's the angle I'm tired to hit.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> What's really changing isn't if something can be done, but rather:<br /> <br /> - Making it Lasting, not Permanent duration.<br /> <br /> - Protecting against Disbelief and Unmaking.<br /> <br /> - Direct control to define Pattern.<br /> <br /> - Achieving Great Work with fewer successes.<br /> <br /> - Rejecting a Reality Zone.<br /> <br /> - Taking down the last hardwired limitations. </div> </div> </div>Of those, mostly I would go with the last one &quot;hardwired limitations&quot;, more or less.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> My suggestion: tackle those directly. Rather than focus on conceptual explanations, Mages have a hard time even explaining such a level because it's actually defined in game terms as operationalizations over the usual rules. It csn also include passive effects, like Diff reduction for other levels.<br /> <br /> Let's write down what the rules say on how Magic works, and how Archmastery can mess with basic definitions. </div> </div> </div>Well, I can see that the initial idea has sort of cast a shadow of doubt, so maybe I should proceed with a few other Spheres, and then I'll be able to better and properly make my case, as you'll all see the overall &quot;theme&quot; I'm aiming here<br /> <br /> Then we can get back to the Life 6, but yes, indeed it has been one that I felt a bit less satisfied with.<br /> <br /> So now I'll proceed with Matter and Mind 6, I think those will make it much more clear on what I'm trying to do and help illustrate my ideas, it will also quench Ramnesis curiosity because, indeed, Matter 5 already gives the impression of covering up everything there is to cover about Matter and doesn't seem to go more fantastic than that, so explain how it COULD go even beyond I believe makes this exercise a bit entertaining.<br /> <br /> And I promise to try to do a better editing of the content.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4e","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/29126-phooku","name":"Phooku","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":1,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2026"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-08-10T16:45:03-07:00","id":1562991,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1562938-archmagic-levels?p=1562989#post1562989\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">TL; DR:<br /> <br /> 1. Don't copy AI. Link if you want, but no copy.<br /> <br /> 2. The game is ontological by default.<br /> <br /> 3. All this stuff is solidly Life 5.<br /> <br /> 4. Only limitations are Mythic Threads, and for thematic reasons.<br /> <br /> 5. What we can improve are Disbelief, ease of attaining Lasting effects and scaling.<br /> <br /> 6. <i><b><span style=\"font-size:14px\">Main</span> <span style=\"font-size:14px\">question</span>: <span style=\"font-size:14px\">what</span> <span style=\"font-size:14px\">do</span> <span style=\"font-size:14px\">we</span> <span style=\"font-size:14px\">get</span> <span style=\"font-size:14px\">out</span> <span style=\"font-size:14px\">of</span> <span style=\"font-size:14px\">this?</span></b></i><br /> <br /> 7. Sphere level may be the wrong approach.<br /> <hr /><br /> I have to agree with <u><b>Heavy Arms</b></u>. I'm mostly in board with using AI as a brainstorming phase tool, if not the only one, but copying the AI and calling it a day is kind of a dick move.<br /> <br /> My suggestion in such moments is that you write a briefing and link the AI chat, that's at least more honest, then you hammer things down later.<br /> <br /> Ontological changes here are meaningless, the AI likes the word &quot;ontological&quot; and misses that the game deals with ontology by default all the time. A Pattern is basically an &quot;ontology unit&quot;, Paradigms are ontological conceptualizations of Magic, and the great tension of the game is how to reach true knowledge if your presence overrides ontological facts.<br /> <br /> The game already cover all limits of possibility at rank 5 making stuff that violate fundamental rules, even before that, revising all examples I see no reason they shouldn't be possible at 5.<br /> <br /> <u><b>Ramnesis</b></u> already touched the simplest way to describe the actual remaining limitations: the Mythic Threads, things that are arbitrarily out of reach for game reasons.<br /> <br /> And with <u><b>Aleph</b></u>'s contributions my point stand simplified: what's left to do is just to mess with Disbelief and clearer and simpler rules to make it Lasting, plus better scaling. Most examples are just that.<br /> <br /> What's really missing is the last question Heavy Arms asked: what does it accomplish for the game? Not how they're more powerful, but why to have them? What you want those Archmages to add to the story?<br /> <br /> To be blunt, my only idea for now is making for Splat Originators, which I'm quite unsure if it is a useful goal. Or Mages capable of rewriting over the Consensus in a definitive way, totally superseding it, which I also fear may be just a bad idea.<br /> <br /> Better scaling, clearer ways to make it Lasting and resistance to Disbelief may be worthy additions to the game, but not necessarily as a superior Sphere level. Either as rules revisions or new Backgrounds that require Arete 6+.</div> </div> </div> </div>Very well, if you guys want to see the full discussion, here it is<br /> <br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"https://chatgpt.com/share/6a7a61ed-e48c-83e9-bcab-668edb9ac73f?ogimg=plain\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/google-material/image_placeholder.svg\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://chatgpt.com/share/6a7a61ed-e48c-83e9-bcab-668edb9ac73f?ogimg=plain\" target=\"_blank\"> </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://chatgpt.com/share/6a7a61ed-e48c-83e9-bcab-668edb9ac73f?ogimg=plain\" target=\"_blank\"> https://chatgpt.com/share/6a7a61ed-e48c-83e9-bcab-668edb9ac73f?ogimg=plain </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> It is... Kinda long thou, and full of my ramblings and the back and forths of it but alas, suit yourselves. I wanted to put out the &quot;highlights&quot;, the resumed points of the conversation, but feel free to tackle it at its fullness","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4e","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/29126-phooku","name":"Phooku","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":1,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2026"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-08-10T16:51:30-07:00","id":1562992,"title":"","content":"So, I can, again, sum up all the conversation in case you guys don't really want to read a book of conversation with AI, but I just have to go to work for now so I'll do it later, just let me know if that's the case","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/29126-phooku","name":"Phooku","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":1,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2026"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-08-10T18:15:03-07:00","id":1562996,"title":"","content":"Just make your posts. The important part is the result, the link is just reference.<br /> <br /> I read something and I think you fell in some pitfalls, but I'll judge better by the actual final text.<br /> <br /> Going by Life I still don't buy it, and I think your response to Heavy Arms sheds more light on the problems than anything, but I need proper final thoughts on other Spheres to see if what I expect to be a pattern will hold.<br /> <br /> On the laziness, you said it yourself: in this case is unforgivable. You shouldn't have just copied the AI, and since it's your post, it's your error to own. The chat is a tool, the nonsense is yours to deal with, not mine to filter.<br /> <br /> And in case Heavy Arms rips you a new one or someone flags you and Moderation takes action, sorry but you have it coming.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-08-10T18:54:31-07:00","id":1562997,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1562938-archmagic-levels?p=1562996#post1562996\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Just make your posts. The important part is the result, the link is just reference.<br /> <br /> I read something and I think you fell in some pitfalls, but I'll judge better by the actual final text.<br /> <br /> Going by Life I still don't buy it, and I think your response to Heavy Arms sheds more light on the problems than anything, but I need proper final thoughts on other Spheres to see if what I expect to be a pattern will hold.<br /> <br /> On the laziness, you said it yourself: in this case is unforgivable. You shouldn't have just copied the AI, and since it's your post, it's your error to own. The chat is a tool, the nonsense is yours to deal with, not mine to filter.<br /> <br /> And in case Heavy Arms rips you a new one or someone flags you and Moderation takes action, sorry but you have it coming.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'll edit things out once I return from work and... Have some time<br /> <br /> To sum it up a little bit, just throw a few things a came up with, such as:<br /> <br /> Prime 6: change the structure of magic itself. So, for instance, you could create a D&amp;D Vancian style of magic, upon which magic doesn't flows from the Avatar and is shaped by will and belief, but rather it comes from gestures and words and components; so, it's the exact gestures and words that become the source of magic, not avatars; this doesn't mean a GLOBAL thing, it doesn't mean that suddenly WoD turns into D&amp;D however, but the Archmagus could turn one individual into a D&amp;D Wizard, or create an area with D&amp;D wizardry.<br /> <br /> It also goes with what I had said about &quot;Industrial Magi-Tech&quot;: for instance, if you manufacture a blaster pistol under *these* particular schematics, than that exact configuration becomes the source of the magic; it's NOT an enchanted blaster pistol, the configuration becomes a magical feature.<br /> <br /> So, at Prime 6 you're basically rewriting (even if only locally) what even Magic is. So, even Sleepers could use these NON ENCHANTED blaster pistols (all they have to do is press the trigger), and the pistols will fire hot plasma.<br /> <br /> Then, I add the suggestion that THIS could be what the Technocracy do, so that would all of a sudden create a very important and kind of fascinating niche for archmagi to occupy.<br /> <br /> Spirit 6 I came up with something like &quot;changing what &quot;Spirit&quot; means&quot;. In a practical sense, you could create something like &quot;alternative Umbra&quot;. Or, layers of &quot;trans-dimensions&quot; that are NOT part of the current Umbra - or whatever the current cosmological architecture of your current universe.<br /> <br /> So, you could create &quot;spirits&quot; that can't really be detected by normal spirit 1 - probably, I'd have to think that one out - or at least not by other spirits. Werewolves certainly wouldn't be able to interact with those, because they don't exist in any sort of conventional &quot;spirit place&quot;, but rather in an entirely artificial new &quot;quantum vibration&quot;.<br /> <br /> It also allows Mages to go beyond &quot;just&quot; the Deep Umbra.<br /> <br /> In theory for instance, you could go to the world of Lord of the Rings. Not an Umbral reflection, not a dream mirror or some such, but the REAL Middle Earth, ruled by Eru-Iluvatar and with its own cosmological rules.<br /> <br /> A tangential consequence of Spirit 6 would also then be &quot;Vampires with Avatars&quot;, since now you can touch Avatars since you can reach for &quot;dimensions&quot; beyond just the Umbral ones","signature":"","edited":{"userid":29126,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/29126-phooku","user":"Phooku","date":". 08-10-2026, 09:59 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/29126-phooku","name":"Phooku","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":1,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2026"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-08-10T22:27:25-07:00","id":1563001,"title":"","content":"Let me try to make my case better on Life 6, this time with my words; but first, while yes, Life 6 under these ideas would cover HEREDITY, which is not covered under any other previous levels, I do have to remark that in my opinion this is more due to a poor construction of the previous levels. <br /> Sure, that alone could merit the lvl 6, but only insofar as previous levels don't cover that adequately, so that's in my opinion should be seen more like a bug than feature.<br /> <br /> Therefore, in my humble opinion heredity should be a parameter for levels 2 to 5 of life; I mean, even sleepers can make square watermelons by genengineering them (and I'm talking in the real world).<br /> <br /> The lack of heredity for previous levels is baffling to me<br /> <br /> That being said, again, although heredity can be one of the cornerstones of Life 6 given the imperfect current mechanics, I do believe that something else should be added to give it teeth.<br /> <br /> So, that is how Life 6 should allow for &quot;creating life that doesn't behave like normal life&quot;. This is NOT creating &quot;living metal&quot; (although I do have something to say about it) or &quot;living plasma&quot; (although I also have the same remarks about that).<br /> <br /> After all, &quot;living metal&quot; is Life 5 + Matter 5, and &quot;living plasma&quot; is Life 5 + Forces 5<br /> <br /> Now, there were a few examples of what I meant above, so I'll revise them for clarity.<br /> <br /> Non Darwinian Life - Lamarckian Evolution <br /> Living beings inherit characteristics of their parents; those aren't however based on the &quot;phenotype&quot;. These are &quot;intrinsic&quot;. If you don't want to go full scientific, in order to keep up with the moto of &quot;science is real, but so too is witchcraft&quot;, you could say that living beings have a &quot;Logos&quot; or whatever, something intrinsic, which is what is passed on, in case you don't want to go full &quot;DNA molecules&quot;. <br /> <br /> But even the most anachronistic mage you could possibly imagine, one stuck on the dark ages living in cave and healing people by &quot;balanced their humors&quot;, who never heard about molecules in his life, even such a person would agree that, simple observation of the natural world can lead us to the conclusion that an amputee won't (necessarily) have descendants that are born without the same limb as the one that individual lost.<br /> <br /> But Life 6 can definitely change that, and create a truly non-Darwinian species<br /> <br /> This could even create some truly amazing and Sci-Fantasy stuff, like a race of cyborgs, whose offsprings are born with machine parts that are assembled from the mother's womb<br /> <br /> Life Assimilation: Science Fiction is filled with aliens capable of consuming other living beings and &quot;assimilating&quot; some of their characteristics. Such is the case of Xenomorphs from Alien, the Zerg Swarm from StarCraft, the alien race of the Kroot from Warhammer 40k and a few others. This is definetely Life 6 territory.<br /> <br /> What's more, usually those are races that can then also spread those assimilated characteristics to their descendants, so once again the non-Darwinian Evolution could be applied, combining the two.<br /> <br /> Non Conventional Life: up here I would put all the Living Metal, Living Plasma, Telepathic Frogs and others.<br /> <br /> There is a caveat thou: any of those CAN already be made with Life 5.<br /> <br /> This, however, is the one case upon which I would say that it is legitimately merited to have Life 6 apply to the need of turning this into a new SPECIES, rather than just simply a highly exotic individual.<br /> <br /> That's because those are configurations that SHOULD NOT BE ALIVE. Life 5 can make an exotic individual made of those, because it gives the &quot;metal&quot; or &quot;plasma&quot; the capacity to behave as a living pattern (have metabolism and what not).<br /> <br /> However, to make it into a new SPECIES, it is required to actually rewrite the rules of what even can be a living pattern, and that's the important part - rewrite the rules.<br /> <br /> So, Life 6 Matter 5 can create a species of Living Metal; Life 6 and Forces 5 a species of Living Plasma to go inhabit stars; and Life 6 Mind 3 a species of telepathic space frogs (because telepathy is supernatural feature - supernatural being, by definition, that which cannot occur naturally).<br /> <br /> Life 6 + Prime 6 could create species of magic beings - for example, bees that produce honey that is Tass, therefore bees capable of processing organic/inorganic matter and turn it into quintessence, and maybe several other &quot;magic abilities&quot;, as long as you add the appropriate Spheres.<br /> <br /> So there you have it, this is what I think for Life 6<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/29126-phooku","name":"Phooku","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":1,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2026"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-08-11T11:27:17-07:00","id":1563013,"title":"","content":"TL; DR:<br /> <br /> You can do everything you said with rank 5.<br /> <hr /><br /> So:<br /> <br /> 1. Prime 5 creates Sorcery Paths. You can reformulate one as Vancian, this isn't against the rules, just a design challenge.<br /> <br /> 2. Locally making blasters actually work is the purview of Reality Zones. The game has the concept and Mages already build them. Doing so is outside Prime 5 only insofar as messing with Consensus and Reality Zones through the direct use of effects is against its themes, but it is theoretically possible.<br /> <br /> 3. Similarly there's no indication that the Union needs much to make their Device factories. It's a minor, albeit fundamental to the lore, mystery how they do that, but probably a combination of Prime 5, Primal Utility 5, Reality Zones and a lot of logistics. Maybe also Entropy 5.<br /> <br /> 4. Turning a schema or blueprint into a working process is a combination with Entropy 5 (target a concept).<br /> <br /> 5. Making alternative Umbrae is already Spirit 5 and several Realms are built close to that, with the possibility of going that far being perfectly within the rules.<br /> <br /> 6. Any world can exist in the Outer Umbra/Space/Horizon and/or as an Everett Volume. It's also doable with plenty Spheres at 5.<br /> <br /> 7. Spirit 5 is also enough to make souls, ghosts and Avatars. What it doesn't do is control such things in sufficiently reliable way to overcome the themes of the game: making the Awakened or any Major Splat isn't a feat above the rank 5 of Spheres, it's just hard and mysterious as a setting convention.<br /> <br /> 8. Heredity is within Life 2, idk why you think it isn't. The rules for Duration and Lasting effects are the only hurdle, plus targeting if the ST feel like it.<br /> <br /> 9. There's zero reason to have non Darwinian evolution (itself a misnomer) outside Life 5, maybe even 4. You are not required to follow laws of biology with Life Magic.<br /> <br /> 10. For Life Assimilation I'd at most require Prime if the method requires Quintessence of a Thaumivore.<br /> <br /> You are running over and over into the same trap: those things are within Rank 5, what's in the way is Disbelief, Duration or Scale. Or even nothing, the game never actually forbade.<br /> <br /> Still in the first exchanges with ChatGPT I saw the warnings about where this would end. The AI told you in the way AI tells, and then went with your vibe because that's what the AI do. You talk to it expecting a continuous line of thought, but the AI doesn't have one, it starts anew at every exchange using context just as a rough guide.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-08-11T12:40:10-07:00","id":1563016,"title":"","content":"<i>About the need of ArchSpheres.</i><br /> <br /> As I see it,, most people don't need them because of how WoD handles rare high tier NPC as &quot;narrative tools&quot;. In normal play, Archmasters are forces of nature that break the basic rules of the game to create plot hooks for the PC. This is represented, like with every other god-tier entity on other splats, as just part of the narrative - they're an extention of the ST. While this ain't everyones cup of tea, it's backed on how WoD it's intended to work.<br /> <br /> A system becomes more of a necessity if one wants to have <i>PC</i> creating new Splats and rewirting reality at massive levels, so I would design it with <i>player characters</i> in mind.<br /> <br /> If one wants this, one way of tackling it it's making Spheres above 5 to handle powers that are beyond the scope of normal play. Archspheres. I doubt it's the best way ... but it's the &quot;way of the books&quot;, and of this thread. <hr /><i>About allowing to change the system</i><br /> <br /> Soo...As an ST, contemplating PC having this power, I wouldn't want to play by a new rulebook each time a player casts a spell. So this needs to have some limitations. I would like such endeavors to be epic enough in scope to have weeks of real-life time to plan and scheme (and limit) the new sub-system.<br /> <br /> Maybe you can import the Awakening idea of Quintessence, and say that to do spells this grand you need to live a story as a prerequisite. That the &quot;effect&quot; it's now a &quot;story&quot;, colours the effect, allows to limit it organically depending of the sub-feats the Mage had to do to get to the point of &quot;casting&quot;. And gives the ST real time to build the Effect.<br /> <br /> Also, that would achieve one of what I consider to be the biggest debts MotA has on it's Archspheres - the idea that you should replace &quot;rote&quot; with &quot;story&quot;, because &quot;there's no rotes for levels this grand&quot;. I don't feel that's true for MotA levels, but it can be done. <hr /><br /> <i>At least for Life, MotA seems to have all those bases covered?</i><br /> <br /> For all it's maligned as simply giving you buffs, the philosophical idea of changing a fundamental fact of the &quot;object of study&quot; at an abstract-level it's very much already on MotA. And it's one of the few parts that I think were, at least, <i>interesting:</i> <b>the existence of meta-patterns</b>. I actually liked this MotA idea, because these are closer to the idea of &quot;platonic ideals&quot; than normal patterns.<br /> <br /> And, in the case of Life, reading the levels up to 8 of Arch-Life with an open-minded eye, I would argue they allow to do what you're suggesting as Life 6.<br /> <br /> MotA Life 6 allows to create completely new and fantastical types of life (On M20 that's part of lvl 5, but I think Revised Life was a bit more limited?)<br /> <br /> MotA Life 7 allows to access the &quot;meta-patterns&quot; of Life, allowing for Effects that are &quot;infectious&quot;, that spread trough the individuals of a single &quot;meta-pattern&quot; - by doing that, and defining the rule of contagion as &quot;reproduction&quot;, you can easily build a new species (it's also possible to <i>alter </i>a whole species).<br /> <br /> MotA Level 8 allows to create lifeforms that absorb the characteristics of what they eat, as part of &quot;allowing Life patterns to exist within patterns, combining them&quot;.<br /> <br /> And, I think that covers everything<br /> <br /> <b>Now</b> of course one could argue that, after shaving the levels and powers that are superfluous, 7 and 8 could be collapsed on a single level. Buuuut that would require a sufficently simple and short writeup as to make it worth to borrow.<br /> <br /> *If anything, I think you could borrow and toy with the concept of <b>meta-pattern</b> to make your Spheres (at least for the pattern spheres). I think it could make it easier to understand than ontological manipulation, as it's more in-line with the rest of the terminology of Mage <hr /><br /> *<i>An example of borrowing the concept of Quintessence, using the Spirit 6 idea about the creation of a new layer of the Umbra.<br /> <br /> As </i><a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar5826_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"5826\" data-vbnamecard=\"5826\">monteparnas</a> said, the power of Realm creation has all you could want roughly covered - conceptually. If we consider that the <i>concept</i> of Realm can be so vast as to cover the <i>whole of ficional worlds created by humanity</i> on <i>one </i>of them you can see it can be ludicrously vast as a concept.<br /> <br /> To the point that, can we <i>really </i>say that the <i>entirety of the Umbra</i> it's bigger than <i>that </i>singular Realm <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> ?<br /> <br /> So, to some extent, everything below could, also, just be covered by increasing the Scope of the magick (tho to a point that would make Mastery 5 Demon Lords blush). But I've already imagined it, so here goes nothing:<br /> <br /> Realms can already change how the rules of reality work and everything. But a whole World, such as the Underworld, it's a place that doesn't have <i>only </i>it's own distinctions and substances (as a Realm can have) but also it's the seat for Realms and higher powers, and also something that permeates adjacent worlds.<br /> <br /> <i>You're not creating an &quot;other world&quot; or an &quot;after life&quot;, you're creating a canvass for &quot;other worlds&quot;</i><br /> <br /> The story could be something akin to wanting to integrate some entities to the spiritual side of the cosmos. Maybe some extraterrestrial species have come to our universe from beyond, and their disconnection to the rest of the cosmology it's causing trouble for them. The Archmages would have to understand these entities - how they are different?. Maybe they aren't born to die, but rather appear as a fully formed potential that gets deconstructed 'til it's born - they don't have an after-life but a source of infinite potential. And not having access to it it's preventing more from forming.<br /> <br /> Now, we could just enter some conceptual plane that has some resemblances (maybe the Radiance?), yank a bit of essence and craft a cozy hideout, but it may not be big enough to handle all their gods and all the ways they relate with their source. To trully make it so there's a conceptually rich world for them, we determine it's Spirit 6 time. It's <i>probably </i>going to involve other Spheres, unless it's supposed to be a blank canvass of spirituality transmuted from some other plane<br /> <br /> Then you have to get the ... we can't call it Quintessence, let's call it &quot;Monad&quot;: That could be gotten by traversing the World Tree asking several deities to give the &quot;seal of aproval&quot; for the new branch, or even &quot;stealing the fruit to plant a new tree&quot; - only after you get the &quot;Monad&quot;, which works as a fulcrum for spells that can't be sustained by a mortal Avatar.<br /> <br /> Meanwhile we can OOC craft the World, and think about how it will interact with the rest of the cosmology, how it's Realms look like, and so on and so forth.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1683,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","user":"Aleph","date":". 08-14-2026, 08:56 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","name":"Aleph","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3056"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-08-11T13:13:08-07:00","id":1563017,"title":"","content":"Well, my post was greened after changing an <i>s</i> for an <i>a</i>, and writting <i>a </i>in the reasons. Maybe I should have given it to the AI to correct the grammar and syntax <br /> <br /> TLDR, I was trying to set some fundaments and ideas to craft Archspheres. <br /> <br /> They have to be of use to all players . On that end I like the <i>great</i> idea of Quintessence Awakening had to make Arch-effects into stories. That regulation mechanism it's good enough I sort of want to use it <i>by itself</i>. Of course, the Spheres can't be ported, and having Archspheres isn't the only way to integrate it on Ascencion. And I thinkered a bit with the idea of creating a new layer of the Umbra as per the OPs idea for Spirit 6<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">1. Prime 5 creates Sorcery Paths. You can reformulate one as Vancian, this isn't against the rules, just a design challenge.</div> </div> </div> </div>We actually had debated on this forums how to create a Vancian-ish system, spells by spell, at even less. Roughly the idea was as this:<br /> <br /> Extrapolating the obscure rules from the Book of Secrets about crafting <i>abstract </i>Grimoires. Basically, if Grimmoires can be immaterial objects like web apps or a song, why not other Wonders?. And why not - say- mental objects on a memory palace or similar?<br /> <br /> Since the magick doesn't require much more than the medium being accessible, it could go as low as Prime 2/Mind 3 to &quot;solidify&quot; and &quot;enchant&quot; a mental construct built into your dreams/subconscious as a Charm (that can be then &quot;used&quot; when you follow the instructions, and it vanishes). With higher levels of Prime you could have stuff that can be passed along and used more than once.<br /> <br /> It would take LONG and a lot of resources - only a Technocrat could do it &quot;alone&quot; with their &quot;facilities&quot;. But, then, you would trully want to put your name on the spell - trully Vancian :P<br /> <br /> *But there's one thing Prime can't do, conceptually, up to 5:<i> Bestow Dynamic Magick</i>. You couldn't, say, give someone Sphere-like powers by crafting Sorcery Paths for them to learn. Which it's something some Demons can do (from Infernalism: Path of Screams, if I remember it right).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","name":"Aleph","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3056"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-08-11T13:25:48-07:00","id":1563018,"title":"","content":"And now that I think about it, if Enchanting and Alchemy are valid Sorcery Paths. Why not a similar road with rituals to create and use Vancian-like spells? Trully, it was there all along...all we would need to think it's some limitations and actual rules to it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","name":"Aleph","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3056"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-08-11T14:57:09-07:00","id":1563020,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aleph</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1562938-archmagic-levels?p=1563018#post1563018\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And now that I think about it, if Enchanting and Alchemy are valid Sorcery Paths. Why not a similar road with rituals to create and use Vancian-like spells? Trully, it was there all along...all we would need to think it's some limitations and actual rules to it.</div> </div> </div> </div>Already possible.. sorta. Sorcerers can hang spells and Willpower acts like spell slots. They also need Quint or Tass to do it, and all rolls have +1 difficulty per two spells hanging.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Custom Sorcery: <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1487084-pattern-weaving-ananasi-sorcery-homebrew\" target=\"_blank\">For Ananasi</a> | Mortal:<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1509365-hekau-for-sorcerers\" target=\"_blank\"> Hekau</a>, <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1550552-ma%C5%A1ma%C5%A1%C5%A1%C5%ABtu-mesopotamian-sorcery\" target=\"_blank\">Ma\u0161ma\u0161\u0161\u016btu</a> | Necromancy:<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1513911-have-you-your-players-ever-used-disciplines-sorcery-for-scholarly-pursuits/page2#post1514352\" target=\"_blank\"> Dust Path</a>, <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1535508-dav20-older-lamia-lore?p=1536244#post1536244\" target=\"_blank\">P.o.Fertile Grave Soil</a> | Thauma: <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1513911-have-you-your-players-ever-used-disciplines-sorcery-for-scholarly-pursuits/page2#post1515316\" target=\"_blank\">Ars Notoria</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27477-voidshaper","name":"voidshaper","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27477_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"698"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-08-11T17:07:02-07:00","id":1563024,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1562938-archmagic-levels?p=1563013#post1563013\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">TL; DR:<br /> <br /> You can do everything you said with rank 5.<br /> <hr /><br /> So:<br /> <br /> 1. Prime 5 creates Sorcery Paths. You can reformulate one as Vancian, this isn't against the rules, just a design challenge.<br /> <br /> 2. Locally making blasters actually work is the purview of Reality Zones. The game has the concept and Mages already build them. Doing so is outside Prime 5 only insofar as messing with Consensus and Reality Zones through the direct use of effects is against its themes, but it is theoretically possible.<br /> <br /> 3. Similarly there's no indication that the Union needs much to make their Device factories. It's a minor, albeit fundamental to the lore, mystery how they do that, but probably a combination of Prime 5, Primal Utility 5, Reality Zones and a lot of logistics. Maybe also Entropy 5.<br /> <br /> 4. Turning a schema or blueprint into a working process is a combination with Entropy 5 (target a concept).<br /> <br /> 5. Making alternative Umbrae is already Spirit 5 and several Realms are built close to that, with the possibility of going that far being perfectly within the rules.<br /> <br /> 6. Any world can exist in the Outer Umbra/Space/Horizon and/or as an Everett Volume. It's also doable with plenty Spheres at 5.<br /> <br /> 7. Spirit 5 is also enough to make souls, ghosts and Avatars. What it doesn't do is control such things in sufficiently reliable way to overcome the themes of the game: making the Awakened or any Major Splat isn't a feat above the rank 5 of Spheres, it's just hard and mysterious as a setting convention.<br /> <br /> 8. Heredity is within Life 2, idk why you think it isn't. The rules for Duration and Lasting effects are the only hurdle, plus targeting if the ST feel like it.<br /> <br /> 9. There's zero reason to have non Darwinian evolution (itself a misnomer) outside Life 5, maybe even 4. You are not required to follow laws of biology with Life Magic.<br /> <br /> 10. For Life Assimilation I'd at most require Prime if the method requires Quintessence of a Thaumivore.<br /> <br /> You are running over and over into the same trap: those things are within Rank 5, what's in the way is Disbelief, Duration or Scale. Or even nothing, the game never actually forbade.<br /> <br /> Still in the first exchanges with ChatGPT I saw the warnings about where this would end. The AI told you in the way AI tells, and then went with your vibe because that's what the AI do. You talk to it expecting a continuous line of thought, but the AI doesn't have one, it starts anew at every exchange using context just as a rough guide.</div> </div> </div> </div>Pretty much this. There's a reason my own attempt at Archmasters operates more along the lines of \u201cLevel 6 lets you do anything that fits the purview of the Sphere but is expressly forbidden even at level 5; but since that's a vanishingly small list of things (as in, I have yet to find an example of this), the main benefit of Archspheres is to make it easier to generate successes, and therefore to perform large Feats.\u201d It doesn't really let you do more things (because by the time you reach the fifth level, there basically aren't any new things to do), so the only thing left is to make it easier to do what you can already do.<br /> <br /> For what role Archmasters play in the game, I'm inclined to borrow heavily from <b>Imperial Mysteries</b>.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-08-12T07:49:29-07:00","id":1563027,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1562938-archmagic-levels?p=1563024#post1563024\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Pretty much this. There's a reason my own attempt at Archmasters operates more along the lines of \u201cLevel 6 lets you do anything that fits the purview of the Sphere but is expressly forbidden even at level 5; but since that's a vanishingly small list of things (as in, I have yet to find an example of this), the main benefit of Archspheres is to make it easier to generate successes, and therefore to perform large Feats.\u201d It doesn't really let you do more things (because by the time you reach the fifth level, there basically aren't any new things to do), so the only thing left is to make it easier to do what you can already do.<br /> <br /> For what role Archmasters play in the game, I'm inclined to borrow heavily from <b>Imperial Mysteries</b>.</div> </div> </div> </div>Imperial Mysteries did a great job of finding a place for Archmages, though it took advantage of Awakening's metaphysics to do so. There, Archmages aren't just defined by their power, but by their relationship to the Supernal. They are on a different place on their journey than other mages. Archmages in Ascension are more powerful, but they are not inherently further on the way to Ascension. Now there is a similar conceptual space in Ascension: mages who are further along in the path to Ascension, who interact with typical mages in limited and inscrutable ways, and who are capable of things that other mages are not... but those are Oracles, not Archmages.<br /> <br /> That said, the other thing I like Imperial Mysteries for was in describing a system and an approach to magic at Archmage levels that was more than just regular magic with a lot of dice. It took the really big world altering spells and broke them down into quests and feats. It even made those into elements lower powered mages could participate in (and political reasons to have them do so) so that there was a place for the typical game to interact with these new elements. That part is the part I think would work well in Ascension and would be a fitting role for Archmages. What would be the main in game motivation for them acting that way, do you think?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage: The Ice-ension: An Epic Game of Reality on the Rink","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/758-ramnesis","name":"Ramnesis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar758_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2220"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-08-12T13:50:43-07:00","id":1563040,"title":"","content":"Unfortunately I didn't read Imperial Mysteries yet, but I think that a system that transforms rolls into quests is ideal.<br /> <br /> For role, that would make Archmasters a focal point for feats that either aren't covered by the Magic System or are hard to judge/make with it, but that exist or may exist within the setting. Things like:<br /> <br /> -&gt; Producing a new Nightfolk, splat or subsplat,<br /> -&gt; Enshrine an Effect as a Cosmological Constant,<br /> -&gt; Create or change a Reality Zone,<br /> -&gt; Terraform a big Realm or area within a Realm,<br /> -&gt; Develop production systems like the Union Factories,<br /> -&gt; Induce one or more Awakenings or restore an inverted Avatar.<br /> <br /> Those are the supposed big feats in Magical History that can't be easily replicated in current rules. They don't require such rules, but making a clear system would make it easy to introduce in a game, either as a plot point or PC initiative.<br /> <br /> As the highest level feat, this system doesn't need to be easy to complete successfully, just easy to map into game sessions. We could have PCs studying these to help Archmages, or for political games where factions dispute the risks and benefits of one such project. They can suggest Effects and try to reach the higher ups, or they can help with or sabotage others. If they reach this level, they become the ones deciding what to try and coordinating efforts, have to gather supporters, and deal with the results of Effects so sweeping they inherently can't control where they go, the effect is now an autonomous phenomenon.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-08-12T14:58:44-07:00","id":1563045,"title":"","content":"Hmm\u2026 so, in a nutshell, Archmastery lets you rewrite Cosmological Constants/Earthly Foundations? That <i>is </i>definitionally something that even Mastery of a Sphere canonically cannot do. Changing a Reality Zone so thoroughly that a Rote doesn't just become Coincidental; it becomes <i>natural</i>, and no longer requires Magick to perform (Prime); altering a Bygone so that it no longer is subject to Disbelief (Life), or purging a subject of Permanent Paradox. Destroying something so thoroughly that it <i>ceases to ever have existed </i>in the first place (Time). Creating a portal between Earth and the Umbra that <i>isn't</i> Vulgar (Spirit). Altering a Reality Zone so much that water runs uphill <i>without </i>involving magick. Extending the scope of a Sphere so that its Effects are worldwide (Correspondence).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-08-12T19:56:18-07:00","id":1563047,"title":"","content":"Basically that.<br /> <br /> Merely as a new Sphere level and regular rules, I'd say it's ridiculous. But as a more involved system where an entire story is built around it, potentially involving lots of people, we can have a lot of leeway without breaking the game or its assumptions: Archmastery is fundamentally distinct from regular Magic, and the effects are by definition possible, despite powerful.<br /> <br /> Lesser effects can happen a number of times in a game with intense, but shortish stories, while world-changing ones would take most of the remaining chronicle, making the disposition of the group to commit to the story a natural check on abuse.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-08-13T06:33:42-07:00","id":1563055,"title":"","content":"This is taking Archmastery to a place where it starts breaking away from the Spheres in general, which might be a good thing. Shifting Reality Zones, for instance, is something that should be at least theoretically possible without Spheres at all, but in all other ways fits into the framework of long term stories and questing that we are talking about for Archmagic. So much so that if we had a good framework for Archmagic, I suspect I'd want to use it for Reality Zone shifts whether any magic rolls were made or not. The way I see it, we could use the Archmagic system even if no Archmages were involved. <br /> <br /> Obviously it depends on what the actual system is.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage: The Ice-ension: An Epic Game of Reality on the Rink","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/758-ramnesis","name":"Ramnesis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar758_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2220"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-08-13T07:47:44-07:00","id":1563059,"title":"","content":"I think that the idea <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/758-ramnesis\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar758_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"758\" data-vbnamecard=\"758\">Ramnesis</a> had of making Mythic Threads can become a step on to this goal from a Lore standpoint.<br /> <br /> A Mythic Thread it's a bit of a confusing artifact that has been various different things. AFAIK, it has been defined as undercurrents of &quot;subconscious&quot; consensus, but also as real supernatural power (for instance, the idea that Kinfolk mages can &quot;mimic&quot; some Gifts w/o Paradox, or bestowing Garou with effects mimicking Gifts w/o Paradox, because they could be able to access those &quot;naturally&quot;).<br /> <br /> But, in any case Mythic Thread it's already a force that runs contrary to the &quot;common sense&quot; of Reality Zones and such. A consensus within the Consensus, or otherwise a form of &quot;reality&quot; that doesn't answer to the rest of reality - like a under current within the current of a river.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">-&gt; Producing a new Nightfolk, splat or subsplat,<br /> -&gt; Enshrine an Effect as a Cosmological Constant,<br /> -&gt; Create or change a Reality Zone,<br /> -&gt; Terraform a big Realm or area within a Realm,<br /> -&gt; Develop production systems like the Union Factories,<br /> -&gt; Induce one or more Awakenings or restore an inverted Avatar.</div> </div> </div> </div>Depending on how we define mythic threads, much of these things could become a function of making or altering these undercurrents. I.E. if a mythic thread can empower static magick, you could make a Splat that violates the Consensus w/o having to deal with Unbelief and such.<br /> <br /> *If the powers of splats <i>form </i>a mythic thread maybe things like removing the Curse of Caine can be done by &quot;tugging&quot; (not even <i>altering</i>) on the thread itself (Like, one of the ideas of the Red Sign it's a ritual that enacts a &quot;play&quot; where the vampire to be cured it's Caine asking forgiveness - it's breaking a Cosmological Constant, but it's not going really contrary to the story of it)<br /> <br /> *The production systems of the Union could be a function of RZ, and thus also a byproduct of MT, but also could be a byproduct of their Paradigm. I guess it's <i>possible</i> we could re-define these &quot;bonuses&quot; sometimes Mages get for being part of a faction (such as this big one, or Do) as a sort of Arch-spell that targets the Paradigm itself - like, when ItX &quot;discovered&quot; mass production he was actually founding this posibility of building Wonders w/o having to spend Wilpower or personal Quintessence<br /> <br /> *I'm not sure about Reality Zones: These are sort of the opposite of Mythic Threads. The latter sort of exists so you can ignore the former. I think an Archmaster needs to be able to make stuff that defy Paradox, but I'm not sure an Archmaster needs to be able to create or change RZ - ultimately all Mages can do this already simply by existing and working on a place (when you make a Sanctum, you're creating a small Reality Zone)<br /> <br /> *Realms do seem to have a relationship with existing concepts, so a Mythic Thread could go as part and parcel with creating big ones, tho it's uncertain how much the Realm existing it's what empowers the concept or the other way arround<br /> <br /> *Avatar stuff doesn't seem like it can be integrated this way. Tho they are mysterious enough that, to some extent, anything goes. <hr /><br /> But, more than justifying effects by themselves, I think this concept can be applied for a system that transforms rolls into quests : A Mythic Thread it's already a sort of narrative, so it could inform to some extent the kind of Stories needed to fuel the effect. You're tasked with building and empowering over a legend that can sustain your mojo, then you can make said mojo.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1683,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","user":"Aleph","date":". 08-13-2026, 10:50 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","name":"Aleph","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3056"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-08-13T10:18:31-07:00","id":1563064,"title":"","content":"Mythic Threads aren't necessarily the only thing Archmastery can do. In this tangent the main point is Magic Through Stories, Effects whose Magic is in the quest to produce them, not in a Ritual roll. That's why I'd lump RZs and Avatars into it rather than just run Mythic Threads/Cosmological Constants/Earthly Foundations.<br /> <br /> I'd slightly counter the notion of MTs running against a RZ by stripping factual effect from in-game theory:<br /> <br /> Some phenomena seem to exist independently from local reality. The Curse of vampires is one of those, but so is Gravity. It's unknown if they share nature/cause, or if different reasons can exist for something to transcend local reality.<br /> <br /> What we know is that there's a Global Plastic Reality (which we commonly term Consensus), a Local Plastic Exception (the Reality Zone) and Non-Plastic Phenomena (which we have 3 names for with theoretical distinctions baked in).<br /> <br /> All that said, most Effects for Archmastery will squarely deal with the third, but dealing with the other two isn't necessarily out of reach, especially when we consider that history within the setting has shown that current theories are either flawed or incomplete: the cause of the Consensus may not really be any consensus or human belief at all, and this ambiguity must remain.<br /> <br /> For Reality Zones, Archmastery can serve as a framework for altering them even if not being their cause. It can also be one possible cause, so a single Mage establishing a house-size RZ isn't incompatible with an Archmaster making a Town-size RZ. This isn't a statement on the nature or source of RZs, but a tool to model in the rules the process of establishing a large RZ or Realm (we have suitable rules for minor ones, but they scale poorly).<br /> <br /> Let me see if I can find and get Imperial Mysteries, if anyone can summarize the rules here it would be nice. For now, what can we use as the fundamental units of story and effect for this rule?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-08-13T11:59:27-07:00","id":1563067,"title":"","content":"It's been a while since I read Imperial Mysteries, but as I recall there's a setting element and a metaphysical element that make archmagic what it is. The metaphysical element is an extrapolation of the Arcane XP system. The learning and discovery that makes Arcane XP what it is can actually be turned directly into fuel or the workings of archmagic. But at such rarified levels it can't be just be any experience, it has to be specific ones. Archmages are advanced enough in their craft that they know what will get them what they need, but it is often incredibly esoteric stuff like the sound of a heart breaking written for a four string quartet, or the specific DNA sequence of a frog in suspended animation in a Siberian glacier, etc.<br /> <br /> The setting element is a cold war/detente among the various archmage groups that keeps them relatively subtle. Ostensibly they are supposed to not rock the boat and keep the world the way it is. In practice, all of them are working both to advance their agendas in the world and to cast world shaking spells that will change everything and propel them further on the path to the Supernal, they just have to be careful and discreet. What this means for magic is that they can't spend much time looking for these unique spell components in the world and instead have to farm that out to younger mages. Likewise other tasks they might need, such as moving ley lines and changing resonances (I forget if thats an Awakening thing) are likewise better farmed out.<br /> <br /> The point is that the spell is broken down and major parts of the effort are taken out of the hands of a dice roll and into the hands of a story that more standard level characters can participate in. And while the specific ideas like Arcane experience don't have a counterpart in Ascension, the idea of searching for key information, specific favors and agreements, vital and unique components, and shifting resonance can.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage: The Ice-ension: An Epic Game of Reality on the Rink","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/758-ramnesis","name":"Ramnesis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar758_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2220"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-08-13T12:32:36-07:00","id":1563070,"title":"","content":"There are basically three parts to it, as I remember: <br /> <br /> 1. A system that lets you spend Arcane Experience on the casting of a spell to \u201csupercharge\u201d it, gaining access to drastically improved Imperial Spell Factors such as number of targets, range, duration, intensity, etc. Basically, gives the Archmaster a way to flex on something regular mages can do. <br /> <br /> 2. Imperial Practices. Awakening uses \u201cPractices\u201d as part of its Arcanum system, where a Practice is a generalized answer to \u201cwhat can you do with X dots in an Arcanum?\u201d which then gets specialized by the choice of Arcanum.<br /> <br /> For the sixth dot, the Practice (I forget its name) allows you to imbue the spell with a sort of intelligence, allowing it to respond to changes of circumstances without having to be \u201cprogrammed\u201d.<br /> <br /> For the seventh dot, there are two Practices: Entities and Excision which do opposite things (kind of like \u201cMake\u201d and \u201cUnmake\u201d), both of which involve altering the nature of a supernatural template as it manifests in the subject of the spell. Cast this on a vampire, and you can add or remove features to it from \u201cwhat does it mean to be a vampire?\u201d Or even to flat-out add or remove the template, turning an ordinary mortal into a vampire or vice versa. And to drive the point home, it goes on to list which Arcana are needed to me with each gameline's template. <br /> <br /> For the eighth dot, you get to me with the environment in a similar way, adjusting what amounts to the fundamental laws of reality within the area affected by the spell. <br /> <br /> I forget what the Imperial Practice for the ninth dot was; but I seem to recall it being something to the effect of being able to simulate the achievement of Ascension. <br /> <br /> 3. Acts of Imperium. This is where the \u201cstory generation engine\u201d comes in: the Archmaster defines one change that he wants to make too the fundamental nature of reality; he is given a list of tasks (ranging from \u201clegendary feat\u201d to \u201cdo the impossible\u201d) that he's supposed to complete in order to achieve his ultimate goal; he's encouraged to recruit agents (such as regular mages) to help him complete those tasks, which are designed to create the perception that what he wants to achieve has been achieved. <br /> <br /> Then, after they <i>are </i>achieved, he enters Supernal Reality and engages in an Act of Imperium to shift the Supernal World to match the changes he's brought about in the Phenomenal World. This isn't a solo Act: other Supernal beings join in, either to support his effort or to interfere with it, and a \u201cbidding war\u201d begins between the Archmaster and his allies on the one hand, and those who oppose his goal on the other. If the Archmaster loses, his attempt to alter reality fails; I believe he also risks utter annihilation should he fail badly enough, where he's erased so thoroughly that it's as if he never existed in the first place. <br /> <br /> If he succeeds, he makes the changes that he's arranged to simulate to become real, fundamentally altering the nature of reality and achieving Ascension, becoming a Supernal god. <br /> <br /> Other parts of the book address, in turn, what it takes to become an Archmaster (answer: you must build what amounts to your own personal Watchtower, creating a \u201csite\u201d in Supernal Reality that defines your essential nature and what your magic is like, replacing your former Path with a fully personalized Golden Road), and what you do after you achieve Archmastery (answer: you right in the Ascension War). <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-08-13T17:45:53-07:00","id":1563076,"title":"","content":"So, breaking it down we have:<br /> <br /> 1. A system that uses the regular rules to make specific things otherwise outside the scope of regular rules. The &quot;traditional&quot; approach to Archmastery.<br /> <br /> 1a. Said system recognizes those limits piecemeal and tackle each directly: Adaptive spells -&gt; Splat Building -&gt; Reality Zone -&gt; Something.<br /> <br /> I'm curious to know more about the &quot;Spell AI&quot; feat, less so but still about the last &quot;Something&quot; in the end, as those may be worth replicating.<br /> <br /> 2. A system that let you burn XP to scale up regular factors. I'm not a fan of burning XP, but scaling up factors will be a thing.<br /> <br /> 2a. This is where Earthbound uses Background and, IIRC, Faith. I think Quintessence in large quantities can be a substitute for XP with a caveat: instead of relying just in Quint economy we could work out how channeling so much of the stuff affects the Mage and the area.<br /> <br /> 3. A system that enacts change in a global scale and, if successful, the character &quot;wins the game&quot;, and where we find the Story-fueled Magic we're after.<br /> <br /> 3a. This one seems at first to go a little too far for our goals, although I'd like some examples to be sure of how it works. It may not be as setting breaking as I think.<br /> <br /> One question I have: how common Imperial Mysteries seems to assume Archmages and such level of casting to be?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-08-13T18:59:38-07:00","id":1563078,"title":"","content":"Rare. That's inherent in the fact that all such casting are fueled by a particularly rare form of XP, but even moreso by the fact that said XP has to be tied to a unique McGuffin. <br /> <br /> Personally, I'm okay with &quot;burning XP&quot; systems, as long as what you get out of it is <i>worth</i> burning them. Plus there's the fact that Arcane XP gets increasingly harder to spend the more advanced your mage is, as more and more of the things you can spend them on get maxed out.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-08-13T19:44:25-07:00","id":1563079,"title":"","content":"Not to mention that other Archmages are certain to interfere when they get wind of what is going on. That whole detente thing they have.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage: The Ice-ension: An Epic Game of Reality on the Rink","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/758-ramnesis","name":"Ramnesis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar758_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2220"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-08-13T21:17:30-07:00","id":1563081,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1562938-archmagic-levels?p=1563078#post1563078\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Rare. That's inherent in the fact that all such casting are fueled by a particularly rare form of XP, but even moreso by the fact that said XP has to be tied to a unique McGuffin.<br /> <br /> Personally, I'm okay with &quot;burning XP&quot; systems, as long as what you get out of it is <i>worth</i> burning them. Plus there's the fact that Arcane XP gets increasingly harder to spend the more advanced your mage is, as more and more of the things you can spend them on get maxed out.</div> </div> </div> </div>I do think it may work in Awakening, but there's no Arcane Experience in Ascension, and that's the point: no system is in place to reward you with a game currency for the particular dramatic actions Awakening does.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-08-14T05:49:25-07:00","id":1563089,"title":"","content":"Well, on thing Ascencion has high ranking mages doing all to often it's figthing for Nodes. This is roughly because a whole Node or more need to be dedicated to build and sustain a Realm. But you also have mages building and mantaining &quot;nets&quot; of Nodes to do unusually large magicks - Voormass was collecting the most corrupted Nodes for whatever evil plan he had, that ultimately was ending death forever as a concept. The Batini had their precious Web of Faith, that's more than &quot;just&quot; a collection of Nodes as it <i>has</i> some special effects to it: It's said to be tied to the Keening and to how Mummies recharge Sekhem.<br /> <br /> There is a precedent for Arch-level stuff requiring extraordinarily large sources of Quintessence, and getting it certianly has been part of such stories. Tho I'm not sure how to rule that expenditure.<br /> <br /> I would say it needs to be a bit more involved than just farming Quint from anywhere for a long period of time. Ressonance seems to have a part to play in here.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1683,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","user":"Aleph","date":". 08-14-2026, 09:24 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","name":"Aleph","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3056"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-08-14T06:34:24-07:00","id":1563090,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1562938-archmagic-levels?p=1563081#post1563081\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I do think it may work in Awakening, but there's no Arcane Experience in Ascension, and that's the point: no system is in place to reward you with a game currency for the particular dramatic actions Awakening does.</div> </div> </div> </div>True, we can't port the system in whole cloth, but we can use it as an inspiration. The Arcane XP element isn't the important part anyways. The thing we really want is the dynamic where Archmagic has requirements that take effort and adventures in their own right before the casting can even happen. That doesn't even have to revolve around a strange and esoteric item either. Setting the spiritual landscape of the casting area, gathering Tass of the exact right resonance, scrying out an offshoot timeline where the effects of the spell happened without the spell, and finding scraps of lost magic can all work.<br /> <br /> But even the strange macguffiny element can be ported, we just have to rest it on something in Ascension. One element that might work as a foundation is Unique Instruments, only at this rarified level the instrument doesn't have an affinity to a sphere, it has an affinity to the spell itself. And yes, Archmages have likely started dropping instruments and could probably drop such a specialized one even faster, but they likely have to have at least a little time to study or practice with the instrument first, which is all we really need for the idea.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage: The Ice-ension: An Epic Game of Reality on the Rink","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/758-ramnesis","name":"Ramnesis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar758_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2220"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-08-14T06:36:05-07:00","id":1563091,"title":"","content":"Now that I think about it: Voormass it's sort of working with the IM set of rules already, isn't he?<br /> <br /> He wanted to End Death as his magnus opus (that would have meant he &quot;ascended&quot; if succeeded, well, in his own terms). He needed the weapon of the first murderer to do so. He had to also expend a lot of resources (Not XP, but he had to get a lot of Nodes with a specific Ressonance) AND traveled to a &quot;special realm&quot;(the Shard of Entropy) where he had to figth as bunch of stuff with his allies to reach his goal.<br /> <br /> We're watching that story from the perspective of the mages that aren't archmasters, but Voormass perspective it's basically a IM archmaster doing their thing.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1683,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","user":"Aleph","date":". 08-14-2026, 09:38 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","name":"Aleph","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3056"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-08-14T10:26:10-07:00","id":1563101,"title":"","content":"We're starting to gather some elements we can use as the &quot;cost&quot; of Archmastery Effects:<br /> <br /> - Entire Nodes,<br /> - Large quantities of Tass,<br /> - McGuffing ingredients,<br /> - Unique Instrument,<br /> - Terrain preparation,<br /> - Field research.<br /> <br /> I'll add to the list:<br /> - Painstakingly specific Resonance,<br /> - Witnesses,<br /> - Integration.<br /> <br /> My thoughts on this:<br /> <br /> 1. We can impose specificity at this level. This effect won't require Quintessence, it will require Nodes, Tass and Quint from Avatars in a non interchangeable way.<br /> <br /> 2. Resonance has to be perfected from start to end, in such a way that collecting an ingredient can't be just about getting it, but getting it in a way that reinforces the Resonance in the right direction. Nodes, Tass, ingredient, Instruments, Location, Execution, even witnesses must all fit the spell.<br /> <br /> 3. There must be some way to quantify the more ephemeral ingredients and/or research. I think we can <i>add</i> an Arcane Experience system where the character is awarded similarly to XP until they have all the ingredients.<br /> <br /> 4. Instruments and rituals shouldn't be possible to ditch in this kind of effect. They're part of the Resonance requirement, not just Paradigm.<br /> <br /> 5. Field Research may use the same Arcane Experience system, or may be measured as a number of phenomena to be observed.<br /> <br /> 6. Witnesses add another layer of reasons to have others making stuff for you. It doesn't need to be witnesses to the final casting, but to any momentous step of the process. That way even seemingly unrelated events can add up to the total witness count.<br /> <br /> 7. Integration requires that all the elements fit formally in function, not just Resonance. The final ritual feels as a coherent process that will cause the effect rather than just things lumped together arbitrarily. I'd personally say that the archetypes convened by the casting must also fit the Effect.<br /> <br /> The idea here is that the requirements work as drive for the Archmage to elaborate adventures and seek help, and also as a clear map of when requirements are achieved. It's not just a lot of things to gather, but things that are disputed, must be gathered in the right circumstances, arranged to have the right witnesses, and can't be easily substituted.<br /> <br /> I'd also say that what sets an actual Archmage apart when using this system is how much they decide how to approach the whole thing. For a PC, it means the ST won't devise a story, but rather run the scenario the player built.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-08-18T07:10:59-07:00","id":1563224,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1562938-archmagic-levels?p=1563101#post1563101\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">We're starting to gather some elements we can use as the &quot;cost&quot; of Archmastery Effects:<br /> <br /> - Entire Nodes,<br /> - Large quantities of Tass,<br /> - McGuffing ingredients,<br /> - Unique Instrument,<br /> - Terrain preparation,<br /> - Field research.<br /> <br /> I'll add to the list:<br /> - Painstakingly specific Resonance,<br /> - Witnesses,<br /> - Integration.<br /> <br /> My thoughts on this:<br /> <br /> 1. We can impose specificity at this level. This effect won't require Quintessence, it will require Nodes, Tass and Quint from Avatars in a non interchangeable way.<br /> <br /> 2. Resonance has to be perfected from start to end, in such a way that collecting an ingredient can't be just about getting it, but getting it in a way that reinforces the Resonance in the right direction. Nodes, Tass, ingredient, Instruments, Location, Execution, even witnesses must all fit the spell.<br /> <br /> 3. There must be some way to quantify the more ephemeral ingredients and/or research. I think we can <i>add</i> an Arcane Experience system where the character is awarded similarly to XP until they have all the ingredients.<br /> <br /> 4. Instruments and rituals shouldn't be possible to ditch in this kind of effect. They're part of the Resonance requirement, not just Paradigm.<br /> <br /> 5. Field Research may use the same Arcane Experience system, or may be measured as a number of phenomena to be observed.<br /> <br /> 6. Witnesses add another layer of reasons to have others making stuff for you. It doesn't need to be witnesses to the final casting, but to any momentous step of the process. That way even seemingly unrelated events can add up to the total witness count.<br /> <br /> 7. Integration requires that all the elements fit formally in function, not just Resonance. The final ritual feels as a coherent process that will cause the effect rather than just things lumped together arbitrarily. I'd personally say that the archetypes convened by the casting must also fit the Effect.<br /> <br /> The idea here is that the requirements work as drive for the Archmage to elaborate adventures and seek help, and also as a clear map of when requirements are achieved. It's not just a lot of things to gather, but things that are disputed, must be gathered in the right circumstances, arranged to have the right witnesses, and can't be easily substituted.<br /> <br /> I'd also say that what sets an actual Archmage apart when using this system is how much they decide how to approach the whole thing. For a PC, it means the ST won't devise a story, but rather run the scenario the player built.</div> </div> </div> </div>Regarding the Arcane XP system, I'd say is if the player can't use said points on anything but the spell, its actually immaterial whether you grant a specific amount of points or just count the milestones. I'd skip including the actual term unless you want to bring in the rest of the ideas of Arcane XP.<br /> <br /> The other thing I'd want to flesh out is why witnesses to non casting parts of the Archspell matter, because that's a pretty big break from regular magic and it usually appears arbitrary and clunky when Mage does that. I'd suggest that mages at this level have eyes on them that are not on other mages. This is true in both the mundane sense and the Paradoxical sense.<br /> <br /> In the mundane sense, the various mage factions tend to take notice whenever a mage of that caliber shows up, enough that they keep records to figure out if he's up to something big. Being seen working towards a big spell increase the odds that someone will show up to try and stop it.<br /> <br /> In the Paradoxical sense, there could be specific Paradox spirits that focus on big magic and getting their attention and interference could raise the stakes of the final casting. I like this option because it puts a face to the adversity and a reason why this has different Paradox rules. It also means that the risks are likely to have more character than just a backlash.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage: The Ice-ension: An Epic Game of Reality on the Rink","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/758-ramnesis","name":"Ramnesis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar758_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2220"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-08-18T08:36:17-07:00","id":1563225,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ramnesis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1562938-archmagic-levels?p=1563224#post1563224\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Regarding the Arcane XP system, I'd say is if the player can't use said points on anything but the spell, its actually immaterial whether you grant a specific amount of points or just count the milestones. I'd skip including the actual term unless you want to bring in the rest of the ideas of Arcane XP.</div> </div> </div> </div>Agreed, that's a different houserule.<br /> <br /> If I was to implement something akin to it, I would like to stress out how Ascencion it's different from Awakening: While there's an interesting side on finding new supernatural or weird phenomena, Ascencion it's more about your will vs. reality. Not all mages are devoted researchers of the occult.<br /> <br /> If anything, I would grant it two ways:<br /> <br /> 1) Achieving a &quot;milestone&quot; of your Paradigm. An act your Paradigm designs as <i>meritory </i>and <i>significant</i>. For some it could be discovering a new occult phenomena, for others it could be things like founding a temple, helping a significant number of people, creating a work of art that trully moves people. Some Scientists might find more value in <i>publishing</i> the newely discovered phenomena in a way that can be experienced by others, than on the discovery itself<br /> <br /> 2)Building a new Reality Zone on Earth - one that's bigger than a Sanctum. As it pertains to the Ascencion War<br /> <br /> And, as said, it wouldn't be just a part of the process for Archmagick. But a part of the process of <i>being a mage - </i>just like Arcane XP on Awakening<i>.</i> But I could see an Archmaster wanting to complete a bunch of these to cast.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> The other thing I'd want to flesh out is why witnesses to non casting parts of the Archspell matter, because that's a pretty big break from regular magic and it usually appears arbitrary and clunky when Mage does that. I'd suggest that mages at this level have eyes on them that are not on other mages. This is true in both the mundane sense and the Paradoxical sense. </div> </div> </div>Yeah, I think this element, likewise, has to <i>mean</i> something for Mage's own narrative. What are we trying to achieve with this?.<br /> <br /> Fooling reality by creating a mini Consensus?. There's a place for this on the mechanics about how a Ritual can be made less Vulgar by casting with more than one hundred people...but Arch-feats are almost certainly going to be Vulgar anyway, and I feel like this idea isn't realy present on Archmage-level feats on the Lore.<br /> <br /> Ascencion isn't about replacing a &quot;lower&quot; reality with a &quot;supernal world&quot;. Archmagic could very well be devised to work on Realms where there's no Paradox whatsoever (Deep Umbra, your own Realm), or over entities where the concept of &quot;witness&quot; Ascencion has doesn't work (like affecting how magic works, that would only be witnessed by supernatural beings - and even then only if the change it's obvious). Moreover I can't think a single feat on Ascencion that <i>required </i>this sort of social engineering other than the <i>average</i>, non magical, building of RZs\u200b.\u200b<br /> <br /> If all we want it's to have &quot;engagement&quot; from other actors, then say any feat on this level it's going to have an <i>Opposition</i>. This doesn't need to be something that's caused by the magick itself, but merely a convention coherent with the idea of &quot;replacerote with story&quot;, as stories tend to have an antagonist or at least a significant other.<br /> <br /> You could even have a table with how different rule-breaks could attract different types of opposition, from the Technocracy to other Archmages, passing by Paradox Incarna that care about, say, the &quot;permanence of things&quot; and wants to be sure everything you make it's going to &quot;fit&quot; with the rest of lasting things. Your ways of dealing with these could define things from the type of allies you would want to have at your back, to the kind of weaknesses your newly created supernaturals will have <br /> <br /> Personaly I wouldn't add this as part of the casting itself, it seems more like a narrative suggestion for the ST to enforce - wheter the character casting it's a player or an npc","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","name":"Aleph","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3056"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-08-18T09:31:11-07:00","id":1563227,"title":"","content":"The option that struck me as the most interesting was the idea of embedding your Focus in the Tapestry so deeply that your Magick doesn't become Coincidental; it ceases to be magical at all, and becomes \u201cjust the way the world works\u201d. Riffing off of Imperial Mysteries, the process would be to first make your Magick Coincidental (say, through a process along the lines of Terranorming), then engage your Archmastery to shift the line between Coincidental and Natural. Or, conversely, shifting the line between Vulgar and Impossible (as far as the Consensus is concerned, of course; mages would see it as \u201cPerma-Vulgar\u201d, to coin a phrase). While Imperial Mysteries phrases it in Awakening terms (altering the Supernal to match the Phenomenal), the premise of actually being able to mold Earthly Foundations/Cosmological Constants/what have you is very appropriate to Ascension.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-08-18T10:07:42-07:00","id":1563228,"title":"","content":"The thing is that, on Ascencion's terms, even if the phenomena created by a spell it's not magical at all,<i> the spell itself </i>should be Vulgar.<br /> <br /> This is <i>often </i>the case when you make Lasting stuff. A fireball it's (unless shenanigans) Vulgar, but the fire caused by it it's Lasting. Healing Aggravated Damage it's Always Vulgar, but the healing it's Lasting.<br /> <br /> Trying to go against a Constant it's supposed to be Always Vulgar. Archmagic it's <i>never </i>said to be &quot;above&quot; this, and I don't <i>see </i>what's the purpose &quot;in game&quot; to <i>make it so</i>.<br /> <br /> In fact, I think it would be <i>bad </i>for the game: This would tempt people to explain the Technocracy making their previously magical technology into mundane stuff as a function of Archmagick. But the whole point of Technocratic Terranorming it's that it's a joint effort of a whole society of mages <i>and </i>mundanes, not the work of some super-mage doing super-magick.<br /> <br /> Well, that's the way I see it at least.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","name":"Aleph","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3056"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-08-18T13:52:53-07:00","id":1563233,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ramnesis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1562938-archmagic-levels?p=1563224#post1563224\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Regarding the Arcane XP system, I'd say is if the player can't use said points on anything but the spell, its actually immaterial whether you grant a specific amount of points or just count the milestones. I'd skip including the actual term unless you want to bring in the rest of the ideas of Arcane XP.<br /> <br /> The other thing I'd want to flesh out is why witnesses to non casting parts of the Archspell matter, because that's a pretty big break from regular magic and it usually appears arbitrary and clunky when Mage does that. I'd suggest that mages at this level have eyes on them that are not on other mages. This is true in both the mundane sense and the Paradoxical sense.</div> </div> </div> </div>On the Arcane XP I agree. The placeholder name is more for now to keep in mind that those milestones will be tracked similarly to XP related ones.<br /> <br /> As a third metaphysical reason for witnesses, I'd say the way it interferes with reality demands a level of subconscious participation from others, be them Awakened or Sleepers.<br /> <br /> You're priming them to expect that something big is going to happen, moving the undercurrents of Belief and Paradigm. If the Consensus is indeed what the main factions believe it to be, you're preparing the terrain for it to accept the Archspell as part of reality. If it isn't, you're still harvesting what Willworking energy exists in the population that witnesses your efforts.<br /> <br /> Partly the Archmaster has moved beyond the Will to change reality, into harnessing the will of the Collective Unconscious to change reality.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aleph</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1562938-archmagic-levels?p=1563225#post1563225\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> If anything, I would grant it two ways:<br /> <br /> 1) Achieving a &quot;milestone&quot; of your Paradigm. An act your Paradigm designs as meritory and significant. For some it could be discovering a new occult phenomena, for others it could be things like founding a temple, helping a significant number of people, creating a work of art that trully moves people. Some Scientists might find more value in publishing the newely discovered phenomena in a way that can be experienced by others, than on the discovery itself<br /> <br /> 2)Building a new Reality Zone on Earth - one that's bigger than a Sanctum. As it pertains to the Ascencion War<br /> <br /> And, as said, it wouldn't be just a part of the process for Archmagick. But a part of the process of being a mage - just like Arcane XP on Awakening. But I could see an Archmaster wanting to complete a bunch of these to cast.<br /> <br /> ...<br /> <br /> Personaly I wouldn't add this as part of the casting itself, it seems more like a narrative suggestion for the ST to enforce - wheter the character casting it's a player or an npc</div> </div> </div> </div>I have the opposite view, hear me out.<br /> <br /> The milestones (we can call them Arcane Milestones, or maybe Reality Milestones) are not meant here as a house rule for extra points in the game, but specifically as a means to quantify the strength of the &quot;story cost&quot; of the Archspell.<br /> <br /> Whatever arbitrary quantity we set, it is filled by achieving a story, even if the character interprets this abstraction as something else. Did the adventure so engaged accomplish its goal? Was it enjoyable by everyone at the table? Someone had an opportunity of learning and growth thanks to it? We may add as many as we want, the point is to have a clear parameter for the preparation, evolution and completion of the Archspell.<br /> <br /> Similarly to the Witnesses cost, I think what makes the Archspell different isn't how much story the ST puts on the way (the ST doesn't need excuses to create conflict), but how must the Archmage devise their plans to gather the materials and enact the ritual.<br /> <br /> Basically, that's my current reasoning, the rules are not a description of what makes the spell work or the reasoning of the character, but rather guidelines for the player of an Archmage about how their schemes must be, and why in mechanical terms they need to be so complex and high profile.<br /> <br /> That gives a particular and important element of the casting of Archspells: the Archmage as a Mastermind, the power player who moves the pieces in accord to an inscrutable plan that only near the end has an understandable form, and the Archspell as a Great Work in a whole new way of putting it, the climax of a mini chronicle or epic story.<br /> <br /> And also because it would be cool for players of Archmages to mess with the idea of being partly ST while for once the rules take from the shoulders of the ST the sole responsibility to make the whole plot, instead working how the plot of the character develops.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1562938-archmagic-levels?p=1563227#post1563227\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The option that struck me as the most interesting was the idea of embedding your Focus in the Tapestry so deeply that your Magick doesn't become Coincidental; it ceases to be magical at all, and becomes \u201cjust the way the world works\u201d.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's my thought. This level of power is the result of a process where the Archmage is messing with the Tellurian in its deepest level. It's not mundane Reality Zone creation, but it's not regular Willworking, it is what happens when you combine both to make your vision be part of reality fully. Something either process alone would stumble on each other and struggle to make any progress.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aleph</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1562938-archmagic-levels?p=1563228#post1563228\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The thing is that, on Ascencion's terms, even if the phenomena created by a spell it's not magical at all,<i> the spell itself </i>should be Vulgar.</div> </div> </div> </div>Definitely, and that's the point.<br /> <br /> The Archmage is forced to work this grandiose plan in a way that attracts witnesses and attention, <i><b>knowing this is the most blatant Vulgarity and a Paradox Bomb of epic proportions</b></i>.<br /> <br /> At no point this process will make the casting of the Archspell Coincidental. Rather, it will be so obscenely Vulgar we need distinct Paradox rules because the usual rules can't take care of something this size.<br /> <br /> Paradox spirits of great power and awareness (or something resembling awareness) are on the move. Mere preparation is requiring Vulgar castings here and there that also feed the building of Resonance, in a sense they may be like valves to release the Paradox of the final result in smaller batches to prevent a Paradox nuke of self-defeating catastrophy proportions. Bizarre phenomena start to happen that other Mages can't understand or link, but are titanic Paradox Effects shifting Reality.<br /> <br /> Our only form of &quot;shielding from Paradox&quot; will be in the sense of making it less story stopping. When Paradox kills a Mage or shuts them out of Reality this ends a story and make for a tragic conclusion rather than an epic one, even if <i><b>to</b></i> an epic climax. We have to avoid the rules getting in the way of the goal, Archmages should survive a successful casting as default assumption (even if in practice unlikely with all the stuff they'll bring upon themselves).<br /> <br /> But other than that? I'd say an Archspell doesn't have a Coincidental option. That would be &quot;not using a spell&quot;, it's rather decades of mundane high level conspiracy and revolutionary change to local Paradigm.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-08-21T06:48:01-07:00","id":1563302,"title":"","content":"Well, the Archmaster as a Mastermind idea it's something I can get behind. Theres definitely enough &quot;going on&quot; with each instance of something that could be regarded as &quot;archmagic&quot; on the Lore to think that there's some level of manipulation that goes beyond your normal ritual.<br /> <br /> I would say it would be better to be flexible about these beats or &quot;Archane Milestones&quot;, maybe some work involves a lot of people and not that many resources, maybe another involves a lot of resources and not that many people. Maybe some requires both...<br /> <br /> *A Wittness in this case would be abstracted, and it would be whomever it's actually relevant for the casting. It doesn't need to be &quot;humans&quot;, but it does need to have a Will. I.E: On the Deep Umbra it could very well be whomever resides on the Realm of application.<br /> <br /> As an example using the Canon: Voormass spell to kill death doesn't really involve a lot of social manipulation, but it's happening at a very specific apocaliptic event where people it's starting to Awaken in large groups, and it's stated that Voormass requires to invoke and move the Will of all these Awakened Avatars with his RItual to succeed - so, those are the &quot;Wittnesses&quot;: The Avatar collective that's being &quot;moved&quot; by the Instrument that's the Ixos Knife on a specific juncture where this is possible.<br /> <br /> *Perhaps it's would be better to drop Witness as a word because it has already implications on Mage, that aren't the same implications we want to use here. I would suggest something like &quot;<i>Backers</i>&quot; instead, as in they got your back (wheter they know it or not) with their Will.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1683,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","user":"Aleph","date":". 08-21-2026, 09:50 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","name":"Aleph","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3056"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-08-21T12:51:33-07:00","id":1563311,"title":"","content":"Going through <b>Imperial Mysteries</b> in a little more detail:<br /> <br /> First, becoming an Archmaster isn't as simple as buying a sixth dot in an Arcanum. While you must have achieved Mastery in at least one Arcanum first and must have enough Gnosis to technically be allowed to purchase the sixth dot, actually gaining the sixth dot requires what's called a Threshold Seeking, which is compared to a Second Awakening \u2014 only this time, it's something the mage initiates rather than being something that happens to him. That is, you need the Storyteller's permission to transition from Mage to Archmaster; but the player must ask for it.<br /> <br /> In <b>Awakening</b> terminology, the new Archmaster replaces the Watchtower he Awakened to with a personal one of his own devising. A Watchtower in <b>Awakening</b> serves a similar role to an Avatar in <b>Ascension</b>; and I personally would liken this Threshold Seeking to replacing the Avatar's Essence with something unique to the Archmaster that has the potential to be expanded into the Infinite Essence. This, in fact, would be the goal of Archmastery, something that ordinary mages only whisper about and don't even have the slightest clue as to where to begin.<br /> <br /> The Threshold Seeking doubles as the first act of Imperial Magic performed by the new Archmaster; and as an act of Imperial Magic, it requires a Quintessence to complete. Once we've hammered out what the <b>Ascension</b> equivalent to what <b>Imperial Mysteries</b> calls \u201ca Quintessence\u201d is, we'll know how this part of <b>Imperial Mysteries</b> would best be adapted to <b>Ascension</b>, assuming we want to adapt it.<br /> <br /> Upon completing the Threshold Seeking, the mage gains a sixth dot in an Arcanum and replaces his Watchtower with a Cintimani. Translating to <b>Ascension</b> terminology, the mage gains a sixth dot in a Sphere, and replaces his Avatar Essence with a custom Essence, which he will subsequently flesh out as his Arete increases until he Ascends and it becomes the Infinite Essence. <hr /><br /> <br /> The first application of the power of Archmastery has to do with \u201cspell factors\u201d \u2014 a system that <b>Awakening</b> developed out of <b>MRev</b>'s \u201cdividing successes\u201d mechanic, and which resembles the Aspects used in <b>SRev</b> and <b>M20 Sorcerer</b>. It suggests paying an Arcane Experience in order to enhance the effectiveness of the spell. In an effort to Keep Things Simple, I would suggest a simple mapping of how much successes achieve: if an Archmaster pays whatever cost we choose to replace Arcane Experience, one success becomes a Standard Feat instead of a Simple Feat; two successes become a Mighty Feat (normally requiring 5 successes); and every success after that kicks it up the equivalent of another five successes, to Overwhelming Feats for three or four successes, and Godlike Feats for five or more successes. This is <i>extremely powerful, </i>which is why it makes sense for the cost involved to be comparable to spending experience points \u2014 a character resource that's very precious to the player and which the player will think twice about spending frivolously. It might be something like the way the Talisman creation rules require a mage to sacrifice a dot of Willpower to complete the act \u2014 a dot which then needs to be repurchased with Experience Points, making it an indirect XP sink.<br /> <br /> Note that there's no mention of Quintessences here: spending Arcane Experiences to enhance Feats doesn't require that additional hoop to be jumped through. <hr /><br /> <br /> The second application of Archmastery is the Imperial Practices: namely, what the sixth through ninth dot in an Arcanum lets you do that the fifth dot doesn't. I briefly outlined these before. Here, I'll lean more into what the ground rules are. First, using an Imperial Practice is never an instant action; it must be done as a Ritual. This is where \u201cthe Quintessence\u201d comes in, in that Ritual casting in <b>Awakening</b> normally requires a sacrament; for Imperial Practices, this gets replaced by a Quintessence:<br /> <br /> [quote]A Quintessence can be an object, place, person, organization, event or phenomenon. Quintessences do not obey any strict patterns, but archmasters have divined some loose guidelines:<ul><li>The Quintessence for a spell symbolizes how the spell feels to the archmaster casting it. It is the Mystery that allows the Road to be used, not a simple \u201cspell component.\u201d</li> <li>Quintessence for a spell usually serves as a metaphor or symbolic reference to the effect or target of the spell, especially if the spell is cast at sympathetic range.</li> <li>Quintessences often \u201cbalance\u201d the effect sought, not in moral terms but in the symbolic language of the Supernal. Returning someone to life must be paid for with death. Forging a wonder often requires the destruction of another.</li> <li>A Quintessence is a unique Mystery \u2014 anything easily come by to an archmage\u2019s resources is unsuitable. Impossible situations and items are often used.</li> <li>A Quintessence may be manufactured or caused by magic. In fact, much of an archmaster\u2019s time in the Fallen World is spent arranging for future needs.</li> <li>The Quintessence is not usually destroyed when the spell is cast, though many are temporary in nature.</li> <li>The Quintessence is often colored by the archmage\u2019s own attitudes, especially her entente loyalties and Noumenon.\u200b</li> </ul>The developer has described the Quintessence as a McGuffin to be used as a story seed and to give the player something to do while the Storyteller works out the implications of what the Archmaster is trying to achieve and how to address them as the game moves forward.<br /> <br /> Second, an Imperial Practice can never be turned into a Rote: every invocation of an Imperial Practice is a unique action, an improv that can never be repeated. If you use any sort of rules about formalizing particular applications of Magick into something that can be taught or learned, those rules don't apply to what dots 6+ let you do.<br /> <br /> Third, an Imperial Practice, like all Imperial Workings, costs Arcane Experience. And not just one, as with the aforementioned Imperial Spell Factors: as the number of dots in the Arcanum goes up, so does the Experience Cost This is justified in part because the things that Imperial Magic does aren't temporary; and performing an Imperial Practice is akin to buying a Merit or Background.<br /> <br /> My initial thought is to say that the mechanics of performing the <b>Ascension</b> equivalent of an Imperial Practice should be modeled on its rules for crafting a Talisman. Only, the thing you're crafting is considerably more extensive:<ul><li>I would move the ability to craft a Hedge Path to the sixth dot of Prime, on the basis that once a Path exists, it exists globally: it isn't limited to a particular person, place, or thing the way a Wonder would be.</li> <li>The Imperial Practice of Dynamics is an exception to the permanence of Imperial Practices; instead, you craft an Effect that takes on a life of its own:<i> \u201cThis Practice allows archmages to create phenomena that change according to conditions \u2014 chain reactions that follow basic principles in a fractal manner without the caster\u2019s<br /> conscious direction or complex \u201cprogrammed\u201d effects. \u2026 Dynamics can create spells that vary in effect depending on the person encountering them, spells that can repair their potency when degraded, spells that react to conditions, expanding viral effects that change Imago as they spread, and spells that would be beyond the archmaster\u2019s ability to conceptualize the Imago for but use Dynamic properties to include all the permutations of a single cause or effect. Dynamic spells are often only loosely controlled by their casters, if at all. \u2026 An archmaster casting a Dynamic spell can determine general principles and leave the spell to itself by relinquishing spell control.\u201d</i> An example given is using a Time Effect to alter the past; but instead of arranging for a particular change and then guessing what the Butterfly Effect will do to it in the present, the Archmaster specifies what he wants the change to the present to look like, and leaves it to the Time Effect to work out how best to get there.</li> <li>\u200bThe Imperial Practice of Entities lets you target a person or creature and alter its fundamental nature. This goes beyond granting the Enhancement Background to the subject; it lets you transform the subject into, say, one of the Kindred. Not \u201csomething that resembles the Kindred\u201d; an actual vampire who operates exactly like a character from <b>Vampire</b> would. Or you could create a Werewolf, a Mage, a Changeling, or anything else, even a custom supernatural type of your own making. Its counterpart Practice, Excision, would let you <i>remove </i>any of these, curing the vampiric curse and reverting the subject back to a normal human.</li> <li>The Imperial Practice of Dominions lets you create Otherworlds of your own design, or alter existing ones.</li> <li>The Imperial Practice of Transfiguration is also an exception to the permanent role of thumb I mentioned: it's basically a fancy way of saying &quot;and anything else you can think of.\u201d If you come up with an idea for an Effect that doesn't fit into what any of the lower levels allow, Transfiguration allows it.</li> </ul>The equivalent to acquiring \u201ca Quintessence\u201d would be how Talisman creation requires you to incorporate \u201cPrimal Energy\u201d into the Talisman in a Paradigm-appropriate way. Especially at Archmaster levels. You can't just use any Quintessence; it needs to be Quintessence in a form that's appropriate for whatever you're building. I might also require an XP cost or something equivalent (e.g., sacrificing character traits such as Willpower). <br /> <br /> This is getting rather lengthy, so I'll address the Appendix (\u201cImperium\u201d) in a later post. I'll note only that the Appendix is the story generator of the book.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-08-21T16:03:34-07:00","id":1563316,"title":"","content":"The Appendix, in a nutshell: define a Noumenon, a.k.a. the vision of Ascension that you seek, and define three Omens for it, establishing goals that need to be achieved: a Personal Omen (representing a change in either your life or the life of someone you care deeply about); and Earthly Omen (representing a change to life on Earth); and a Celestial Omen (representing a change to the Otherworlds), plus the possibility of one or more Profane Omens (additional goals unrelated to Ascension which must be completed first).<br /> <br /> Each Omen is rated on a five dot scale based on how hard they are to achieve, from Masterful to Epic to Legendary to Godlike to Supreme. For each, design a story lasting at least one chapter and culminating in a challenge requiring you to earn a large number of successes, from 6 (for Masterful challenges) to 10 (for Supreme challenges), with intermediate levels being Epic, Legendary, and God-like. You can reduce the number of successes needed by employing a number of strategies such as splitting the challenges into multiple simpler challenges, employing non-Archmaster agents to complete the stories for you, or employing mortals using non-supernatural means to achieve your goals. It also suggests the Storyteller Adventure System (a tool that Onyx Path developed to help provide structure to story creation) as a way to aid in creating these story arcs. <br /> <br /> If the culminating challenge fails, the Archmaster can search for a replacement challenge; but the replacement has its challenge rating bumped up by one. On a success, the corresponding Omen is sealed, and the Archmaster begins a bidding war in the Supernal World to Exalt the changes, granting them \u201ceternal, universal truth\u201d. For instance, an Omen of \u201cdestroy all vampires\u201d might involve a story that might involve destroying every vampire in a particular region; but once that's accomplished, the Archmaster can Exalt it, and suddenly the world as a whole changes so that vampires do not exist, and never have. (\u201cDestroy all Witches, in this world and every other, past, present, and future.\u201d) Exalting an Omen is retroactive and universal. <br /> <br /> Exalting an Omen is a bidding war between the Archmaster and his allies on the one hand, and those who oppose the Omen on the other hand. The \u201cbargaining chips\u201d in this bidding war are earned through the performance of Imperial Practices, after which careful application of the accumulated resources determines, without dice, whether or not the Omen is Exalted. Part of the challenge here is that you can come up short, but you can also overshoot your goal. Both are bad, leading to unintended consequences. If you're getting too close to succeeding, an enemy can disrupt your effort by pushing you to go too far instead of merely trying to restrain you. <br /> <br /> Once every Omen has been Sealed and Exalted, the Archmaster Ascends.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-08-21T17:51:30-07:00","id":1563318,"title":"","content":"In the<b> Ascension</b> version of this, the stories for Earthly Omens should frequently revolve around Reality Zone Shifts/the Terranorming process. The effects of Exalting the corresponding Omen would be to push already-Vulgar Effects that the change discouraged into Earthly Foundations territory, meaning that shifts in the Consensus are no longer capable of making them Coincidental; such features are now \u201clocked out\u201d of the Tapestry, and can only be performed by mages willing to risk the Paradox of a Vulgar Effect. Conversely, Coincidental Effects that get pushed towards being accepted cease to be Magickal at all: the Effect is woven directly into the Tapestry, not just the Consensus, and <i>anyone</i> who performs such a Rote in accordance with the Practice being pushed, using the Instruments associated with it and rolling a dice pool based on the Ability associated with it can successfully generate the Effect; they don't even need to invest in a Path of Sorcery to do so.<br /> <br /> Unless Archmastery levels of Time are involved, the change <i>isn't </i>retroactive; and unless Archmastery levels is Correspondence are involved, the change isn't universal either. But otherwise, Exalting an Omen would work just like it does in <b>Imperial Mysteries</b>.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-08-21T19:30:16-07:00","id":1563323,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aleph</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1562938-archmagic-levels?p=1563302#post1563302\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I would say it would be better to be flexible about these beats or &quot;Archane Milestones&quot;, maybe some work involves a lot of people and not that many resources, maybe another involves a lot of resources and not that many people. Maybe some requires both...<br /> <br /> *A Wittness in this case would be abstracted, and it would be whomever it's actually relevant for the casting. It doesn't need to be &quot;humans&quot;, but it does need to have a Will. I.E: On the Deep Umbra it could very well be whomever resides on the Realm of application.<br /> <br /> ...<br /> <br /> *Perhaps it's would be better to drop Witness as a word because it has already implications on Mage, that aren't the same implications we want to use here. I would suggest something like &quot;<i>Backers</i>&quot; instead, as in they got your back (wheter they know it or not) with their Will.</div> </div> </div> </div>My idea for now is that the Archmage starts a work by designing the effect, and mechanically that's building an effect and assigning costs, or rather the &quot;currencies&quot; to be used to pay a cost.<br /> <br /> Let's say a given effect costs 15 [Arch Points] (a placeholder name). Then we have a chart where [Backers], Witness, Tass, Nodes, Avatar and [Arcane XP] are given [Arch Points] values. The player picks and chooses from this chart to build the cost of the Archspell, but once the cost is settled it must be followed.<br /> <br /> That's the &quot;noninterchangeable&quot; part: you can use Nodes and you can use Tass, but once you define how much of each, this is not reversible.<br /> <br /> And the [Arcane XP] part (I'm thinking maybe a name like Myth Milestones may be better, more precise) is one option, not the generic name for the chart, but the cost paid as story beats rather than story goals.<br /> <br /> I'll try an example. Let's say to the effect above the Archmage chose 5 [Arch Points] in [Arcane XP], and that means 25 [Arcane XP]. It means the Archmage or other participants must go through stories to gather undefined resources, information or whatever, but those stories will contribute to the Archspell based on how much [Arcane XP] they generate in a chart adapted from XP rewards. It could be like the following:<br /> <br /> 1. The Archmage personally took part in the story (1);<br /> 2. A character accomplished a Great Ambition (in line with a Seeking) (1);<br /> 3. An important Flaw from a character or in the plan seriously risked the entire mission, but was overcome through sacrifice or growth (1);<br /> 4. The group recorded a Key Knowledge about Magic, learning something about the cosmos, the nature of True Magic or the Effect (1);<br /> 5. The mission was a partial/full success (1/2);<br /> 6. The whole group survived (1).<br /> <br /> So at the end of a story, the ST judges how it went and awards [Arcane XP] accordingly. It's tallied against the goal (25) until it's met. This way what's being measured as cost isn't a fixed quantity of resources, but the quality of a story told to gather those resources.<br /> <br /> Our player may decide (throwing here arbitrary numbers just as example) the Effect will cost 5 Nodes (1 Arch Point), 50 Quintessence in Tass (2 Arch Points), 25 Quint from Avatars (2 Arch Points), 100 fully Nightfolk [Backers] (3 Arch Points), 10 Sleeper Witnesses (2 Arch Points), on top of 25 [Arcane XP] (5 Arch Points). All of those are story drivers in that the Archmage must plan something to gather such resources, but the Arcane XP is freeform as they plan a number of missions related to the Archspell that are directly judged by story beats.<br /> <br /> We can have Witnesses still as in &quot;witnesses to Vulgar Magic aligned to Archspell Resonance&quot; as one possible element in the currency chart, which would be part of the Paradox of the final Archspell being broken into several obligatory Paradox Events. Or maybe have a similar chart to the above for the Archmage to decide how they'll manage the obscene brunt of Paradox of an Archspell. <hr /><br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1562938-archmagic-levels?p=1563311#post1563311\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Going through <b>Imperial Mysteries</b> in a little more detail:</div> </div> </div> </div>That's really useful, I'll parse my observations on it, and how I think we could translate or not into Ascension. <hr /><br /> I'll cover my take on Quintessence later, but the Threshold Seeking may need a more specific guidance on how to run it than regular Seekings (which are already a confusing mess).<br /> <br /> About the Avatar, I wouldn't go for the Infinite Essence. Instead, I'd ditch Essences altogether for an Arch-Avatar Archetype, which's basically any layer of abstract meaning the player wants to put in it. It can be a Major Arcana, a Jungian Archetype, a TV Trope, anything.<br /> <br /> Drawing on the idea from Ascension that not only Archmastery isn't Ascension, but it may actually run counter it, I'm thinking about this Threshold Seeking being kind of blasphemous: it's using Magic to impose your Will over your very Avatar. It's not literally and or anything, but it's something that fundamentally removes the original role of the Avatar as a guide to Ascend and turns it into an expression of your Flawed self, for whatever that means.<br /> <br /> Going for Archetypes makes it both personal and customizable and easier to grasp, as Mage is already excessively abstract. Archetypes are ready-to-digest abstractions players can plug and play right away yet can elaborate infinitely later. We can then take a page from Spirit Rank in CoD and have the Avatar accumulate a new Archetype for each Arete dot above 5, turning more complex.<br /> <br /> Calling this Seeking/Magic would come either with buying a dot of Arete above 5 (triggering a mixed Seeking) or buying a Sphere dot above 5 (triggering only this Seeking). Unless we decide Spheres above 5 don't follow usual cost, which isn't something I'm against). <hr /><br /> I used Arcane XP as a placeholder for a reason: what it accomplishes in Awakening that I find interesting is it taking a similar kind of effort as regular XP, but is tracked in parallel and gained through additional opportunities rather than using your regular XP.<br /> <br /> For this system, that means spending XP won't put you behind the others as cost to get things done, which is an old pet peeve of mine. I never liked dot costs, by the way. Won't oppose if you insist but the above explanation on [Arcane XP] is my vote for how to systemize this.<br /> <br /> What I'd add: [Arcane XP] accrued beforehand is halved for use. I'm not particularly strong on this limitation, I just think adventures made as part of the quest to get an Archspell done are more interesting than those undertaken just to fill stocks. <hr /><br /> I'd simplify Spell Factors further: spend [Arcane XP] to multiply successes. It can be Quadratic (Success \u00d7 2^N), Geometric (Success \u00d7 1+N) or Geometric With a Toll (Success \u00d7 N). N, of course, is the amount of [Arcane XP] used. We can put a limit equal Arete, Highest Sphere or Lowest Sphere. I'd use Quadratic with limit per Lowest Sphere, but require the use of Dividing Successes when doing so. <hr /><br /> Quintessence in <b>Imperial Mysteries</b> terms isn't a hard concept because Ascension already has the language to describe the idea: Resonance. It's basically every aspect of what the game always tried to explain Resonance as being, minus Synergy.<br /> <br /> My current definition for it: [Core Components] for [Archspells] are Unique Tass or other Quintessence repository that must fit the casting and Paradigm perfectly. Both the Effect and the Tass must share Resonance, and this must fit or bridge somehow the Resonances of the Mage, the target and the goal in some way. Player and ST are free to explore how it works, as long as the result seems logical and add to the themes of the chronicle.<br /> <br /> Tass already can take the other forms cited in the description provided, the only difference is that in Ascension it must carry extra Quint, but I think that's a fitting element for translation, it isn't by itself as inherently strange as it is in Awakening with Mana, and it's doable in many ways. We can work the wording of all options better, but the gist of it is the same. <hr /><br /> Imperial Practices become [Archspells], which are the core of our goal here. I think most of the components and assumptions work well:<br /> <br /> 1. Always ritual, thoroughly agree. You already have [Success Multiplier] as an option that works with improvised casting, [Archspells] not.<br /> <br /> 2. Always require a [Core Component], we may need a system to define how much Quint this Tass must have, just to have a reference of how hard it is to make. Quintessence = Target Successes is probably a good starting point.<br /> <br /> 3. No Rote I agree with a caveat: I think one possible application of an [Archspell] could be the creation of a unique Rote that allows other Mages &quot;merely&quot; at Master level to perform that specific [Archspell], at least while they have the support of the Archmage or some setup they prepared.<br /> <br /> My model for this is Mummy and the Spell of Life. Isis performed the original [Archspell], but the result can be taught to lesser Mages, being one of the few recurring effects in WoD's lore that really requires the Mage to learn a rote. It's improved after the 6th Maelstrom, but we can place Osiris here as an effective Archmage for our purposes. That way Archmages can have lasting impact through Effects that break your normal rules, but aren't individually world shaking if not replicable.<br /> <br /> 4. Agree with [Arcane XP] costs always being required, though I think the best approach is specifically the system I envisioned above in this post. We can set some elements at base levels, you always have to include at least that much of them, and for [Arcane XP] that could be Highest Sphere level minus 5, or just Highest Sphere level if we want to be stinger.<br /> <br /> One aspect to consider, though, is that it's likely that [Arcane XP] will also be used to multiply successes because of Difficulty. Unless we also change the basic spellcasting rules, those spells will have very high Difficulty to begin with, making accumulating successes a heavy task, and many will need a lot of them for [Spell Factors].<br /> <br /> 5. I wouldn't move the creation of Hedge Paths to [Archspells] to avoid messing with what the rules already allow, but I think we can have the imparting of a Path as such an effect.<br /> <br /> The thing with Hedge Paths is that the result is not something that exists, it's something that can be learned by someone else with XP. Who's actually empowering the Path isn't the Mage, it is the hedge magician: they're working hard to master it, spending XP, applying their own will and paradigm. And the Mage has no control on this knowledge, it will spread on its own and be used, abused, adapted and modified however others are fit.<br /> <br /> At heart, even if created by a Mage the Path is entirely a thing if the Sleeper world that follows its regular rules, the Mage was little more than an inspiration. But what about empowering the Hedge Magician?<br /> <br /> With a 6th dot Effect you turn the Path into a middle state between [Dynamics] and [Entities]. A target acquires the Numen at the level defined in the [Archspell], no personal expense (or need for willingness), and the Mage retains some control, or at least an influence as defined by [Dynamics], over the resulting powers and how they'll be used or passed along.<br /> <br /> Creating [Archspell Rotes] could fall here, too, but with the added burden of executing your original spell anyway.<br /> <br /> 6. For the rest, I think the [Practices] are ok. The [Dynamics] is maybe a tad redundant, Ascension has enough space to work something like that at lower levels, but as a more solidly stated effect + clear successes + [Path Imposition] and [Archspell Rotes] it's a solid 6th dot. The rest is good and the whole covers almost everything we could ask for.<br /> <br /> Should we assume ignoring Disbelief and such is inherent to those levels, or add a minor extra rule, maybe a [Spell Factor] for this?<br /> <br /> We could describe those [Practices] in terms of [Constants] to ground into Ascension parlance. 6th dot is [Engraving a Constant in the Effect], 7th dot is [Engraving a Constant in the target], 8th dot is [Engraving a Constant in the Zone] and 9th is [Engraving a Constant in the World]. <hr /><br /> I think the Appendix is too much rooted in the Awakening cosmology, breaking some of the themes and assumptions of Ascension that even Archmages shouldn't. Namely:<br /> <br /> 1. Reality is defined by Consensus. Mages fight over the minds of the masses already because they're the key to it, and causing lasting change at a global scale is the focus of an ongoing war between factions, being simultaneously easier but also vulnerable. No single Mage should be able to overrule the war itself.<br /> <br /> 2. Ascension is not Platonic Gnosticism, the main conflict is open and within reality rather than above it. The thematic thread of its great works is not personal enlightenment changing reality from the supernal, but creating means for others to carry on with the fight for ideals.<br /> <br /> 3. Ascension embraces ambiguity. Mysteries in it are unknowable by definition, never resolving in a definitive answer. Even Archmastery should leave in the air the question: &quot;do I really know how I did that, or is my belief so powerful I can't know the reality behind it?&quot;<br /> <br /> 4. As its main mystery, Ascension can't be given a rule. There may be a Mage that'll ascend exactly as detailed in the Omens system. Most won't, and we'll never know why.<br /> <br /> I'm not against writing down possibilities for Ascension, I actually think its past the time for us to have an entire book on options about how to define Ascension in a chronicle, but the place for this is not the Archmage rules.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-08-21T19:33:08-07:00","id":1563324,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1562938-archmagic-levels?p=1563318#post1563318\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">In the<b> Ascension</b> version of this, the stories for Earthly Omens should frequently revolve around Reality Zone Shifts/the Terranorming process. The effects of Exalting the corresponding Omen would be to push already-Vulgar Effects that the change discouraged into Earthly Foundations territory, meaning that shifts in the Consensus are no longer capable of making them Coincidental; such features are now \u201clocked out\u201d of the Tapestry, and can only be performed by mages willing to risk the Paradox of a Vulgar Effect. Conversely, Coincidental Effects that get pushed towards being accepted cease to be Magickal at all: the Effect is woven directly into the Tapestry, not just the Consensus, and <i>anyone</i> who performs such a Rote in accordance with the Practice being pushed, using the Instruments associated with it and rolling a dice pool based on the Ability associated with it can successfully generate the Effect; they don't even need to invest in a Path of Sorcery to do so.<br /> <br /> Unless Archmastery levels of Time are involved, the change <i>isn't </i>retroactive; and unless Archmastery levels is Correspondence are involved, the change isn't universal either. But otherwise, Exalting an Omen would work just like it does in <b>Imperial Mysteries</b>.</div> </div> </div> </div>Ok, posted before reading this, I can get behind this version for some effects.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-08-22T06:32:19-07:00","id":1563334,"title":"","content":"I think the creation and imparting of a Path could be phrases entirely in terms of Dynamics: the Path is an Archspell that's designed to be passed on to people through instruction or study, and to over the command of the sorcerer that it's taught to. It's never made part of the sorcerer (and therefore doesn't require Entities); it's strictly something the sorcerer <i>has, </i>rather than something that the sorcerer <i>is. </i><br /> <br /> What do you think of my idea of using the Wonder creation rules for Archspells? It's inherently ritualistic, requires massive investment by the Archmaster (simulating the Arcane XP cost), and as you suggested can implement the intent of \u201cthe Quintessence\u201d simply by being very strict as to the Resonance of the Quintessence integrated into the Archspell. <br /> <br /> Spending Arcane Experience as a success multiplier should be severely limited, as it can get wildly out of hand otherwise. Even something as simple as \u201ceach XP spent increases the multiplier by 1\u201d means that spending 4 XP on a casting means that one success is a Mighty Feat, two or three successes are Overwhelming Feats, and four or more successes are Godlike Feats. That's about as far as I'd be willing to push things. <br /> <br /> More generally, I'd prefer to investigate the potential of adding something like an Arcane Experience system to <b>Ascension</b> as its own thing, rather than as an adjunct to Archmastery. <br /> <br /> I agree with your idea about making the shift to Archmastery be a case of changing the relationship between the mage and the Avatar from \u201cthe Avatar guides the mage\u201d to \u201cthe Avatar serves the mage\u201d. This would mean that the \u201cThreshold Seeking\u201d and whatever comes after would no longer be Seekings, as that concept is built around the Avatar guiding the mage. I'm not sure what I'd call the \u201cseize control of your destiny\u201d variant that Archmasters would have, or precisely how it would work. But it provides an easy explanation as to why Archmasters cannot achieve Ascension: they have stopped Seeking it. What <i>they're </i>after is Apotheosis: they strive to become gods. Rephrase everything that <b>Imperial Mysteries</b> has to say about Ascension in terms of Apotheosis. <br /> <br /> And yes, I could see part of that being modeled by the Archmaster developing his <i>own </i>Essence, separate from and effectively replacing his Avatar's Essence (not that the Avatar's Essence changes; it just creates to be relevant to the Archmaster). I do get what you're saying about <b>Mage</b> already being too open-ended; but if there's ever something that needs to be unstructured and intensely personal, this is it. That doesn't mean that there can't be advice given; but it should be the sort of advice found in the Focus rules. In fact, the Archmaster Essence should be related to the Archmaster's Paradigm.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-08-22T08:08:26-07:00","id":1563336,"title":"","content":"Note also that the normal rules for working Effects breaks for Archspheres: at a Difficulty of (3 to 5) plus highest Sphere required, an Effect requiring six dots in a Sphere has a target number of 9 for Coincidental Effects, and the whole thing becomes reliant on Threshold successes beyond that. Plus, as Archspells typically are <i>at least </i>Mighty Feats, you're talking about having to go through this same frustrating exercise potentially dozens of times. And then you're likely to run into the cap on how many rolls you may attempt on a ritual casting. <br /> <br /> If we model Archspells on the Wonder crafting rules (as opposed to just using said crafting rules as written), we could perhaps rejigger things a bit so that the difficulty on the pool is lower \u2014 say, the Archsphere rating itself, \u00b11 for the rare Coincidental it Vulgar with Witnesses situations. So a Dynamics Archspell would have Difficulty 5 to 7, and a Transfiguration Archspell would have Difficulty 8 to 10.<br /> <br /> This makes successes more frequent, which is kind of the point: rolling six to eight dice and <i>maybe</i> getting one success is likely to be deeply frustrating. And that's at the bottom end, where the need for Threshold Successes doesn't consume that success and render a failure. Instead, the challenge of casting an Archspell relies on the number of successes needed, which would traditionally be in the 5\u201320 range per the Feats table, and the Quintessence investment, which is made more scarce through the strict Resonance requirements.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-08-22T09:44:08-07:00","id":1563342,"title":"","content":"I'm not strongly for or against Path creation being at 5th or 6th dot, was just pondering if altering the regular rules should be within the exercise. It may just as well be that Mages with no Archmastery are inspirations, most Paths are actually merit of the magicians who did the hard work to replicate the effect. Archmages can and do make the real deal, though.<br /> <br /> Wonder creation I'll have to reread to be sure, it isn't a rule I use frequently (never got my players to use them much even when they get Prime 5, go figure). But I think it's a solid basis, if one that needs some polish just because it has some weird wrinkles here and there that I think came from a rule originally run more by feeling than hard numbers.<br /> <br /> [Arcane XP] has the advantage for now that we can fine control how it's gained and how much. This has by itself some limiting effect on the spell. If the Archmage needs to dedicate two or three sessions to get 5 points, using that to get 5 successes per actual success isn't as bad.<br /> <br /> But we can use the (Success \u00d7 N) formula and limit by Lower Sphere, cap at 5. I think that's a reasonable starting point for Playtest at least.<br /> <br /> These Archmage rules will also serve as a test field for the [Arcane XP] system, I agree with you. Mage has too steep costs and too much strain on your regular XP that you'll also want to use in mundane things. All splats do, but Mage even more so. And just as in Awakening, this system will let us create inherent rewards for engaging with relevant themes, that work in a consistent manner. We can even have more than one such system for games using other themes.<br /> <br /> On Apotheosis, it's a good idea, but we have to think what it means in the setting and what it doesn't. We have a list of important characters that can be in their path to it or trying to. Has Voormas reached Apotheosis, or would that be if and when he finished his final work? What about Control before Void Adaption? Are the &quot;truly&quot; immortal masters that personally saw a lot of Mage history in Apotheosis or seeking it? Tzar Vargo? Anyone ever truly achieved it, or is Apotheosis still a pipe dream, as rarified or even more than Ascension? I think we need to ponder this, if we should or not point at a char and use as an example of it.<br /> <br /> For giving advice on Apotheosis and Ascension I think the take of Requiem in VII was a good idea: give examples. Make them completely independent takes that may be true or not, but with multiple examples you have a grounded basis to work with without limiting or curbing the much needed individuality.<br /> <br /> Difficulty I always assume the character will try to game some bonuses, and I think Archspells are ones where perfect conditions should be sought after. If the character is rolling one with less than a full -3 Diff modifier, something is seriously off. So I'd say we're actually talking from Sphere to Sphere +2 Difficulty. Even then I concede that we may need some further break in some castings. Diff 7 is still reasonable, Diff 8 means an average 2 successes per roll for an Arete 6 Mage, with reasonable risk of failure.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-08-23T07:14:00-07:00","id":1563367,"title":"","content":"Honestly, I do not like archmastery and I much rather M20 &quot;default&quot; of spheres going up to rank 5. This means that rank 5 is the pinacle of power for that sphere and should be able to do *anything* in that subject.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3153-lord-revan","name":"Lord Revan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3153_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1419"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-08-23T17:32:40-07:00","id":1563390,"title":"","content":"Easy solution: don't use it. The list of things that can't be done at Mastery is short, and consists of things that you probably don't want mages doing anyway. <br /> <br /> The more challenging problem is what to do for those who <i>do </i>want to use it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-08-24T04:28:47-07:00","id":1563402,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1562938-archmagic-levels?p=1563390#post1563390\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Easy solution: don't use it. The list of things that can't be done at Mastery is short, and consists of things that you probably don't want mages doing anyway.<br /> <br /> The more challenging problem is what to do for those who <i>do </i>want to use it.</div> </div> </div> </div>Indeed. I'm sorry if I didn't contribute to the topic, but that's just my feeling.<br /> Also, what things you consider that can't be done? If not using archmastery I would argue that there is no such list. I mean, the list of things you can't do this way also couldn't be done with arch, afaik","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3153-lord-revan","name":"Lord Revan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3153_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1419"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-08-24T05:22:30-07:00","id":1563408,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lord Revan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1562938-archmagic-levels?p=1563402#post1563402\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I mean, the list of things you can't do this way also couldn't be done with arch, afaik</div> </div> </div> </div>They can, if you read the thread you'll see this is the case.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-08-24T07:01:36-07:00","id":1563411,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1562938-archmagic-levels?p=1563408#post1563408\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> They can, if you read the thread you'll see this is the case.</div> </div> </div> </div>My point is that everything that you'd say that fall into rank 6+ would be rank 5. And what shouldn't be, like using magick to increase Arete for example, wouldn't be possible with neither rank 5 or 6+","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3153-lord-revan","name":"Lord Revan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3153_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1419"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-08-24T09:24:02-07:00","id":1563416,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lord Revan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1562938-archmagic-levels?p=1563411#post1563411\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">My point is that everything that you'd say that fall into rank 6+ would be rank 5. And what shouldn't be, like using magick to increase Arete for example, wouldn't be possible with neither rank 5 or 6+</div> </div> </div> </div>And your point is wrong, read the thread.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-08-24T11:33:53-07:00","id":1563424,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lord Revan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1562938-archmagic-levels?p=1563411#post1563411\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">My point is that everything that you'd say that fall into rank 6+ would be rank 5. And what shouldn't be, like using magick to increase Arete for example, wouldn't be possible with neither rank 5 or 6+</div> </div> </div> </div>The thread it's mostly about explaining the OP how rank 5 covers, conceptually, pretty much everything. As you say.<br /> <br /> The real conundrum of what's impossible to mages it's never so much tht there's a &quot;concept&quot; a Sphere doesn't cover yet at rank 5, but more about how the spell would interact with the <i>other</i> rules. Again, as you say.<br /> <br /> Even things that are impossible, aren't really impossible because they're not &quot;covered&quot; in the Spheres but because of accesory reasons. For instance, &quot;curing&quot; a Nephandi. Spirit 5 already allows to create a <i>new</i> soul, in all senses from creating spirits to new human beings. Why not un-twist an Avatar?. Well, because the game doesn't want you to. And because Avatars are supposed to be misterious so maybe there's another element that's missing appart from having total mastery of the soul<br /> <br /> Except then Senex goes and ... maybe? ... does it.<br /> <br /> There are many &quot;feats&quot; on Mage's Lore that are, at least, &quot;sus&quot; on how they were achieved within the rules. The creation of a new splat it's the most common one - not because the creation of someone with magical powers it's &quot;beyond the 5th rank&quot;, but because it would break a lot of rules.<br /> <br /> But still, a wizard did it. She hasn't to explain shit - but players do, and because of that it's interesting to think about a system to &quot;get into the fun&quot;.<br /> <br /> Archmasters exist. This is about tying them to rules rather than leaving them as ST tools. <hr /><br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Should we assume ignoring Disbelief and such is inherent to those levels, or add a minor extra rule, maybe a [Spell Factor] for this?</div> </div> </div> </div>I struggle to see a case where it shouldn't be part of the effect. But maybe it would be better to <i>still</i> make it a Factor, just in case someone can/wants to save a few points by making the spell so it erodes over time outside of it's Zone.<br /> <br /> I'm really liking the system you're building. It seems very modular.<br /> <br /> I like that while Arch-spells are inherently ritualistic there's also an option to &quot;beef up&quot; normal magicks, because part of the identity of Archmasters on Ascencion it's being able to do really potent castings - see Porthos instantly exploding a guardian spirit of Horizon that had over 50 essence (instant powah it's not the only way to explain this, but it's the apparent one on the narrative).<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">What do you think of my idea of using the Wonder creation rules for Archspells? It's inherently ritualistic, requires massive investment by the Archmaster (simulating the Arcane XP cost), and as you suggested can implement the intent of \u201cthe Quintessence\u201d simply by being very strict as to the Resonance of the Quintessence integrated into the Archspell.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think it's a good idea to fuse both systems. Mage has more than enough sub-systems as it is. Less bookeeping it's never not going to be good<br /> <br /> But at the same time I'm not a fan of Wonder creation rules.<br /> <br /> A personal peeve of mine it's that it isn't clear how the power of an effect relates to the cost of the Wonder. This creates a loophole that could be a problem for a system that's mostly about regulating stuff that go beyond the scope of normal magicks, I think.<br /> <br /> But mostly I feel like we would have to add too much to it. There's too much going on in creating a <i>story. </i>For instance<i>: </i>Realm-creation has a requisite wonders don't have: dedicating Nodes. This is actually important for the <i>stories</i> Realms are supposed to tell. Similarly I feel like being specific with Quintessence may not be enough<br /> <br /> I'm almost tempted of proposing the other way arround: Having a general &quot;magick-projects&quot; manual that includes the cappability of the Effect to be &quot;on&quot; and &quot;off&quot; and to react to commands (from the wielder on the case of a Wonder), then limit some Spell Factors (such as, ignoring Disbelief) to people with Arete Levels 6-10.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1683,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","user":"Aleph","date":". 08-24-2026, 03:01 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","name":"Aleph","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3056"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-08-24T13:00:04-07:00","id":1563426,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1562938-archmagic-levels?p=1563416#post1563416\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> And your point is wrong, read the thread.</div> </div> </div> </div>Nah, I'll wait for you to point out where I'm wrong.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar1683_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"1683\" data-vbnamecard=\"1683\">Aleph</a> thank you, that's exactly what I'm talking about. And if &quot;the games doesnt want you to&quot; at rank 5, it most likely won't want you to at rank 6+. <br /> <br /> I do understand those who like archmastery and wants to add it to the game, though. No problem at all, was just giving my 2 cents","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4e","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3153-lord-revan","name":"Lord Revan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3153_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1419"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-08-24T17:45:41-07:00","id":1563439,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lord Revan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1562938-archmagic-levels?p=1563426#post1563426\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Nah, I'll wait for you to point out where I'm wrong.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar1683_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"1683\" data-vbnamecard=\"1683\">Aleph</a> thank you, that's exactly what I'm talking about. And if &quot;the games doesnt want you to&quot; at rank 5, it most likely won't want you to at rank 6+.<br /> <br /> I do understand those who like archmastery and wants to add it to the game, though. No problem at all, was just giving my 2 cents</div> </div> </div> </div>You didn't gave your two cents, you crashed on the parade then insisted in saying something was wrong despite not knowing what it was about.<br /> <br /> Aleph already explained. We're discussing rules to do stuff the usual rules don't allow, for STs who want to play with that. You didn't say anything that hasn't been said by us several pages ago.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-08-25T19:03:50-07:00","id":1563484,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1562938-archmagic-levels?p=1563439#post1563439\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> You didn't gave your two cents, you crashed on the parade then insisted in saying something was wrong despite not knowing what it was about.<br /> <br /> Aleph already explained. We're discussing rules to do stuff the usual rules don't allow, for STs who want to play with that. You didn't say anything that hasn't been said by us several pages ago.</div> </div> </div> </div>I never said something was wrong wtf are you talking about?<br /> I just said that I rather put effects that would go into rank 6+ into rank 5,as M20 default.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4e","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3153-lord-revan","name":"Lord Revan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3153_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1419"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-08-26T19:52:09-07:00","id":1563521,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lord Revan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1562938-archmagic-levels?p=1563426#post1563426\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Nah, I'll wait for you to point out where I'm wrong.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar1683_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"1683\" data-vbnamecard=\"1683\">Aleph</a> thank you, that's exactly what I'm talking about. And if &quot;the games doesnt want you to&quot; at rank 5, it most likely won't want you to at rank 6+.</div> </div> </div> </div>Technically true; but we're talking about a house rule here. What the game does or doesn't want you to be able to do takes back seat to what the house rulers want you to be able to do. And the house rulers have decided that they want to put the stuff the game officially doesn't want you to be able to do at level 6+.<br /> <br /> If you'd read the thread, you'd know that; <i>and </i>you'd know that they started from much the same position that you expressed, before developing the thread in a new direction. Which means that you didn't bring anything new to the thread. Instead, you just popped in and threadcrapped. Again, there's a simple fix for you: disregard the thread; it's not for you. And then there's the slightly harder but likely more rewarding solution: read the thread with an open mind; you just might learn something.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":421,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","user":"Dataweaver","date":". 08-28-2026, 06:46 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-08-26T22:39:26-07:00","id":1563523,"title":"","content":"I'm going to reread the Wonder creation rules now, by the way, to see how we can cannibalize it for our Archmastery system.<br /> <br /> Had to postpone a little due to health reasons that reduced my focus for reading, but I'm getting better.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-08-27T07:08:43-07:00","id":1563533,"title":"","content":"The one thing I think it's interesting about the Wonder system it's that it can add Flaws to the Wonder. There's some narrative place for grand magical projects having weak points or side effects. But I wouldn't copy it. Flaws are here based on Merits &amp; Defects and that's a very poor system.<br /> <br /> However I think <i>the concept of it</i> could be a good idea for Arch-magcik <i>that falls short.</i> After expending all the time &amp; effort required to cast an Arch-spell, if the dice don't accompany we could device a system that allows to succeed anyway, but in exchange of letting the ST take creative control of some of the &quot;factors&quot; and other attributes of the spell, twisting it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","name":"Aleph","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3056"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-09-21T12:58:46-07:00","id":1564250,"title":"","content":"Sphere 6 being the cap and allowing for weird and conceptually experimental stuff is the best way to run arch mastery. I'd agree fully with the op on that except I'd go farther and say there is no sphere 7. They're unnecessary, oracles or whoever is beyond arch masters have the powers of plot. Like Caine they don't have stats.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28924-tjalei","name":"Tjalei","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2025"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"81"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-09-23T00:02:22-07:00","id":1564291,"title":"","content":"I finally managed to finish rereading the Wonder Creation rules. Even managed to finally figure out some old doubts like what's the difference between a living Periapt and a Soulflower.<br /> <br /> For our exercise, what matters:<br /> <br /> 1. Wonder creation breaks the process into 4 phases with distinct rules: Foundation, Energy, Purification and Quickening.<br /> <br /> 2. Difficulty follows normal rules, actually, so we start from 3-5 + Sphere and get modifiers that can sum up to \u00b13.<br /> <br /> 3. It does give greater control over modifiers, though. Purification in particular gives you any opportunity to add a unique-to-Wonders up to -3 Dif modifier, making minimum difficulty way easier to get. It also increase the bonus and penalty from Resonance.<br /> <br /> 4. More importantly, by breaking the process into phases, it eases <i>success accumulation</i>. This is big. Each phase isolates stakes, making for more refined risk management and prep strategies while keeping individual rituals within reasonable targets.<br /> <br /> I think we can use all that in some manner. And the Difficulty part we can tackle by making the Purification-analogue phase count outside the usual limits. So you can only have up to -3 Diff from usual sources, but this phase gives extra -3 that can bring you down to -6.<br /> <br /> Fast break down:<br /> <br /> 1. Foundation uses Ability rolls to build the thing that will be the Wonder. Use whatever Craft system you like.<br /> <br /> 2. Energy requires 5\u00d7level Quintessence plus a Prime effect to lock it in the Foundation. Level of Prime (and so Diff) depends on source. Successes = 3\u00d7level.<br /> <br /> 3. Purification works as 0 to 3 independent Prime 2 rituals. Complexity scale exponentially with number of rituals, but that's fluff. Target successes scale with Foundation complexity and how messy the Resonance is, but no examples are given.<br /> <br /> 4. Quickening requires a ritual to infuse the Effects. Use highest Sphere to set Diff, target successes = 3\u00d7level.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-09-26T07:39:10-07:00","id":1564354,"title":"","content":"Now bear in mind that for Spheres 6\u20139, Sphere+3-to-5 is difficulty 9-to-15; and even that 9 assumes the extremely rare case of an Archsphere being used to work a Coincidental Effect. Maxing out the difficulty reductions, that's Difficulty 6\u201312.<br /> <br /> With the rule that 1s cancel successes, that's a <i>best case</i> scenario of 4 successes per ten dice, which very quickly drops to one success per ten dice; and <i>then </i>you start having to overcome a Threshold, needing an extra one to three hits to get one success. If you <i>don't</i> optimize for lowest possible difficulty, that Threshold can climb to 6 or even 9 additional hits per success, in a range where the total number of hits you're likely to get is <i>maybe </i>one per ten dice rolled, if you're _lucky._ And with a cap on the number of attempts you can make, the upper levels become exercises in frustration <i>even for mages with maxed out Arete. </i><br /> <br /> That's why I suggested recalibrating Archspells to trade off more successes required for rolling at a lower difficulty: so that working Archmagick doesn't feel <i>quite </i>so much like a Sisyphean task.<br /> <br /> (By the way: a reasonable alternative to the Threshold rule would be to stop at difficulty 9 but double the number of successes needed for each step after that. That still means that what would nominally be 18 to 30 successes balloons to 18, 42, 96, 216, and 480 successes, if we don't decide to tone it down.)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":421,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","user":"Dataweaver","date":". 09-26-2026, 12:59 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-09-26T10:23:22-07:00","id":1564361,"title":"","content":"I would say to ignore the Arch-levels, at least on that particular end (if not altogether). Breaking dice mechanics doesn't provide any benefit I can see, the increased difficulty and the need to do extra steps to affront it can be better tackled by the complexity of the requisites of the ritual .","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","name":"Aleph","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3056"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-09-26T11:14:21-07:00","id":1564362,"title":"","content":"The problem is that if you leave the difficulties as 3+Sphere, you're practically <i>forced </i>into Threshold territory. The only way to avoid it is to not go into Archsphere territory. And that pretty much defeats the point of the exercise of identifying things that Sphere 6+ would do.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-09-26T11:43:05-07:00","id":1564363,"title":"","content":"No, and I agree with <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar1683_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"1683\" data-vbnamecard=\"1683\">Aleph</a> in this.<br /> <br /> I just had the same idea: <i>stop</i> <i>Difficulty at Sphere Level 5</i>.<br /> <br /> Just that. The character buys the new levels, we proceed to make the rules, but for Difficulty calculation only it stops at 5.<br /> <br /> That makes perfect sense: our system is already distinct from regular Magic rules, the requisites are greater and so are the successes needed. There's no actual reason for any rule from previous levels to remain if they don't make any contribution.<br /> <br /> We can transfer the increase both to the steep requirements of Archspells or to the number of successes required, as those are subsystems we are making up anyway, so we have the level of control needed to balance things there.<br /> <br /> And I'd say an Archmage is actually likely to roll the final ritual as Coincidental. Sure, the Archspell is too powerful to not be Vulgar for all descriptive purposes. In fact, so powerful we'll have a whole process of dishing Paradox along the way in smaller batches.<br /> <br /> The side effect is that it does free up the final ritual to follow more or less regular analysis. The absurd Paradox was already generated and distributed, the final step is a trickle in comparison, but at least this they can try to damper with a Chantry or Realm. We may not use this, too, and still capping the diff calculation at Sphere 5 is sound.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-09-26T19:48:05-07:00","id":1564376,"title":"","content":"And this is why it's a good idea to bounce ideas off of other people. You're exactly right. The only remaining \u201ccomplication\u201d is that the Magickal Modifiers chart includes a +1 to +3 Difficulty for sheer power (that is, Outlandish to Godlike Feats), which means that you need to come up with more negative Magickal Modifiers to offset them.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-09-26T21:56:24-07:00","id":1564378,"title":"","content":"Add the Wonder Creation Purification or something similar and we can have a manual &quot;add rituals to offset this&quot;.<br /> <br /> In the Wonder Creation rules this was put as a means to offset Resonance problems, as the ST may require a level of specificity for it that's hard to fit, with more serious than usual consequences. Since for Archspells we'll be more demanding with Resonance on purpose, it can offset any extra modifier anyway.<br /> <br /> Just in case it applies to an improvised spell, we can have the Purification be doable with antecedence by working it on your Instrument for a specific later spell or at least specific Sphere and level.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-10-20T15:33:44-07:00","id":1564877,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tjalei</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1562938-archmagic-levels?p=1564250#post1564250\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Sphere 6 being the cap and allowing for weird and conceptually experimental stuff is the best way to run arch mastery. I'd agree fully with the op on that except I'd go farther and say there is no sphere 7. They're unnecessary, oracles or whoever is beyond arch masters have the powers of plot. Like Caine they don't have stats.</div> </div> </div> </div>I agree on lvl 7 being unnecessary.<br /> <br /> There are a few things I thought out for some of the lvl 6. For instance, Time 6, you can remove yourself from the time continuum, which means you could go back in time, kill yourself as a baby and be completely fine, because you're no longer scored in the time continuum.<br /> <br /> Then for Entropy 6, you'd be able to manipulate the PROBABILITY SPACE - not just manipulate probability, but the SPACE - for instance, you could create causes without consequences. A bullet is shot, it hits someone, it goes inside the skull of a person, but since you removed the very probability space of that bullet to cause injury, the bullet simply causes nothing.<br /> <br /> You could also create a superposition of probabilities, by getting a total sum of probabilities to go above 100%.<br /> <br /> Say for example that I determine that the chance a person dies from a bullet is 100%, but the chance that same person survives from that same bullet is also 100%, so now you have 2 outcomes for a total sum of 200% chance of happening.<br /> <br /> You'll force reality into a superposition state, upon which the man you shot is both death and alive AT THE SAME TIME.<br /> <br /> The man goes home have dinner with his wife, but at the same time (and at the same home), the wife is also receiving the news of her husband's murder by police officers.<br /> <br /> With Prime yes, you could make things that are &quot;magic&quot; become simply mundane. Anyone can levitate stuff by saying &quot;vingardio leviosa&quot; at your home because you've re-written the very metaphysics of your place. Levitating stuff using that phrase becomes as mundane as using apps on a cellphone.<br /> <br /> The Mind 6 I based myself on the book 1984 to formulate. You can change concepts GLOBALLY. I would name it &quot;Newspeak&quot;. Just like in the book, the concept of &quot;peace&quot; gets eliminated, and people can no longer think about it simply because the very concept is nonexistent - there's only &quot;war&quot; and &quot;not-war&quot;.<br /> <br /> There's also one interesting example from real life... Portuguese has the word &quot;Saudade&quot;, which is the word used for when someone &quot;misses&quot; something.<br /> <br /> But to &quot;miss&quot; something is a negative feeling - you can only &quot;miss&quot; that which is absent.<br /> <br /> The word &quot;Saudade&quot; however is a POSITIVE feeling - it's even hard to explain in any other language other than Portuguese itself, because no other languages in the world actually possess that very concept of which the word relates to. So, I can't even explain to any others the difference between what the word &quot;Saudade&quot; conveys which cannot be simply covered by the word to &quot;miss&quot; something, because simply put, no other languages in the world even have that very concept.<br /> <br /> So, Mind 6 works similarly - you can create or erase entire concepts of cognitive reality.<br /> <br /> Those are some of the ones I was thinking about","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4e","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/29126-phooku","name":"Phooku","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":1,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2026"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-10-21T00:07:08-07:00","id":1564880,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Phooku</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1562938-archmagic-levels?p=1564877#post1564877\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I agree on lvl 7 being unnecessary.<br /> <br /> There are a few things I thought out for some of the lvl 6. For instance, Time 6, you can remove yourself from the time continuum, which means you could go back in time, kill yourself as a baby and be completely fine, because you're no longer scored in the time continuum.<br /> <br /> Then for Entropy 6, you'd be able to manipulate the PROBABILITY SPACE - not just manipulate probability, but the SPACE - for instance, you could create causes without consequences. A bullet is shot, it hits someone, it goes inside the skull of a person, but since you removed the very probability space of that bullet to cause injury, the bullet simply causes nothing.<br /> <br /> You could also create a superposition of probabilities, by getting a total sum of probabilities to go above 100%.<br /> <br /> Say for example that I determine that the chance a person dies from a bullet is 100%, but the chance that same person survives from that same bullet is also 100%, so now you have 2 outcomes for a total sum of 200% chance of happening.<br /> <br /> You'll force reality into a superposition state, upon which the man you shot is both death and alive AT THE SAME TIME.<br /> <br /> The man goes home have dinner with his wife, but at the same time (and at the same home), the wife is also receiving the news of her husband's murder by police officers.<br /> <br /> With Prime yes, you could make things that are &quot;magic&quot; become simply mundane. Anyone can levitate stuff by saying &quot;vingardio leviosa&quot; at your home because you've re-written the very metaphysics of your place. Levitating stuff using that phrase becomes as mundane as using apps on a cellphone.<br /> <br /> The Mind 6 I based myself on the book 1984 to formulate. You can change concepts GLOBALLY. I would name it &quot;Newspeak&quot;. Just like in the book, the concept of &quot;peace&quot; gets eliminated, and people can no longer think about it simply because the very concept is nonexistent - there's only &quot;war&quot; and &quot;not-war&quot;.<br /> <br /> There's also one interesting example from real life... Portuguese has the word &quot;Saudade&quot;, which is the word used for when someone &quot;misses&quot; something.<br /> <br /> But to &quot;miss&quot; something is a negative feeling - you can only &quot;miss&quot; that which is absent.<br /> <br /> The word &quot;Saudade&quot; however is a POSITIVE feeling - it's even hard to explain in any other language other than Portuguese itself, because no other languages in the world actually possess that very concept of which the word relates to. So, I can't even explain to any others the difference between what the word &quot;Saudade&quot; conveys which cannot be simply covered by the word to &quot;miss&quot; something, because simply put, no other languages in the world even have that very concept.<br /> <br /> So, Mind 6 works similarly - you can create or erase entire concepts of cognitive reality.<br /> <br /> Those are some of the ones I was thinking about</div> </div> </div> </div>Had an archmaster of spirit once long ago who learnt to make localized avatar storms.<br /> <br /> Be in a spiritual realm, cause a small piece of it to splinter, the splinterd cause further splinters, and then it's not a good place to be in anymore.<br /> <br /> Couldn't control the direction of it at all, so it was drop it and run. St was also really vague on how long it would last. The mages version of a nuke pretty much. Used it once in a nephandi realm.<br /> <br /> Other people did other stuff, think one made a dragon out of living fire but might misremember.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28924-tjalei","name":"Tjalei","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2025"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"81"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-10-21T03:09:04-07:00","id":1564884,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Phooku</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1562938-archmagic-levels?p=1564877#post1564877\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I agree on lvl 7 being unnecessary.<br /> <br /> There are a few things I thought out for some of the lvl 6. For instance, Time 6, you can remove yourself from the time continuum, which means you could go back in time, kill yourself as a baby and be completely fine, because you're no longer scored in the time continuum.<br /> <br /> Then for Entropy 6, you'd be able to manipulate the PROBABILITY SPACE - not just manipulate probability, but the SPACE - for instance, you could create causes without consequences. A bullet is shot, it hits someone, it goes inside the skull of a person, but since you removed the very probability space of that bullet to cause injury, the bullet simply causes nothing.<br /> <br /> You could also create a superposition of probabilities, by getting a total sum of probabilities to go above 100%.<br /> <br /> Say for example that I determine that the chance a person dies from a bullet is 100%, but the chance that same person survives from that same bullet is also 100%, so now you have 2 outcomes for a total sum of 200% chance of happening.<br /> <br /> You'll force reality into a superposition state, upon which the man you shot is both death and alive AT THE SAME TIME.<br /> <br /> The man goes home have dinner with his wife, but at the same time (and at the same home), the wife is also receiving the news of her husband's murder by police officers.<br /> <br /> With Prime yes, you could make things that are &quot;magic&quot; become simply mundane. Anyone can levitate stuff by saying &quot;vingardio leviosa&quot; at your home because you've re-written the very metaphysics of your place. Levitating stuff using that phrase becomes as mundane as using apps on a cellphone.<br /> <br /> The Mind 6 I based myself on the book 1984 to formulate. You can change concepts GLOBALLY. I would name it &quot;Newspeak&quot;. Just like in the book, the concept of &quot;peace&quot; gets eliminated, and people can no longer think about it simply because the very concept is nonexistent - there's only &quot;war&quot; and &quot;not-war&quot;.<br /> <br /> There's also one interesting example from real life... Portuguese has the word &quot;Saudade&quot;, which is the word used for when someone &quot;misses&quot; something.<br /> <br /> But to &quot;miss&quot; something is a negative feeling - you can only &quot;miss&quot; that which is absent.<br /> <br /> The word &quot;Saudade&quot; however is a POSITIVE feeling - it's even hard to explain in any other language other than Portuguese itself, because no other languages in the world actually possess that very concept of which the word relates to. So, I can't even explain to any others the difference between what the word &quot;Saudade&quot; conveys which cannot be simply covered by the word to &quot;miss&quot; something, because simply put, no other languages in the world even have that very concept.<br /> <br /> So, Mind 6 works similarly - you can create or erase entire concepts of cognitive reality.<br /> <br /> Those are some of the ones I was thinking about</div> </div> </div> </div>Those are all feasible with level 5. All of them. Some are even actual rotes or effects published in official books. Some actually take even less.<br /> <br /> Removing yourself from time and causality: doable with Time 4, standard with Time 5, a bit of Entropy helps.<br /> <br /> Eliminating consequences or causing superpositions with Entropy just require auxiliary Spheres, but with the right preparation is doable at Entropy 2. At 4 you can do some of those with Entropy alone.<br /> <br /> Making Magical things become mundane is a Reality Zone, you don't even necessarily need Magic, and is a valid effect to request to be available in a Sanctum. Anyway that's not what Prime does, it deals with Quintessence, not with all effects of Magic in a way that you can bypass other Spheres (in this case Forces).<br /> <br /> Changing or removing the meaning of words is squarely Mind 4. Add Correspondence if you want it global with 30 successes rather than a bazillion, but it's there.<br /> <br /> Entropy 5 has the way more interesting effect of removing the concept from reality rather than just from minds. You propose a world where peace is unknown. I propose one where peace is a logical impossibility.<br /> <br /> Also, &quot;saudade&quot; is a perfectly translatable word, it just isn't translatable with one single word on most languages. But the sentiment does exist. The idea that words are a requisite for conceptual perception fell from scientific scrutiny decades ago.<br /> <br /> Saudade is the intense nostalgia you feel when you miss something enough to hurt, although it may be just a little.<br /> <br /> It isn't exceptional, every language is full of tricky words in this vein, and to say no other language at all has an equivalent is bold and probably wrong. It isn't present in the most common languages in Europe and America, though.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-10-21T07:04:09-07:00","id":1564894,"title":"","content":"You can also explain why the word is hard to translate directly. Such as the English word Gobbledygook, which is a very specific shade of nonsensical language because it was invented as a mocking term for deliberately vague and confusing political speech and specifically references the sound turkeys make. That may be too much information to easily work into an actual translation, but it can still be translated and conveyed.<br /> <br /> Also, there is such a thing as close enough. I do suspect that Gobbledygook has such a specific meaning (and lack of meaning) that there isn't a perfect match for it in another language, but how often is that specificity actually required? Or even intended? In every case I've seen the word used a close approximation would convey the intended information, and most languages will have a close enough approximation.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage: The Ice-ension: An Epic Game of Reality on the Rink","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/758-ramnesis","name":"Ramnesis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar758_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2220"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-10-21T07:24:36-07:00","id":1564895,"title":"","content":"As an aside, I really enjoy that for Spanish and Portuguese, the words most known for being hard to translate (Duende and Saudade) have emotional and/or spiritual depth. Meanwhile the correspondingly hard English word is a mocking nonsense word coined to call out other nonsense. My native language has depth, it just doesn't show well here. <br /> <br /> Maybe it's because we are so quick to coin words and phrases. Or maybe it's because English has a modus operandi of shanghaiing the words and phrases from other languages because they fit the zeitgeist or are the mot juste to capture what we are trying to say. C'est la vie.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage: The Ice-ension: An Epic Game of Reality on the Rink","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/758-ramnesis","name":"Ramnesis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar758_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2220"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-10-21T18:44:30-07:00","id":1564904,"title":"","content":"Those are actually all very common through languages. And the main reason we always use Saudade to talk about unique Portuguese word is because it's the most beautiful one.<br /> <br /> I also like how different languages encode subtle but important distinctions in nuance even in analogous words.<br /> <br /> &quot;Cool&quot; in the sense of nice can be directly translated into Portuguese (at least Brazilian) as &quot;legal&quot;. Almost same valence.<br /> <br /> But there is a subtle difference between using a word related to cold to say that, and a word that means &quot;legal&quot;. The implied aspect of low heat, slow motion (metaphorically), calm, is absent in Portuguese.<br /> <br /> The Brazilian equivalent has a more high energy/pitch implication, open expression, or sometimes low-key presence, being usable in more contexts, including formal ones. It's positive in a broader sense.<br /> <br /> One multi-word term in Portuguese that's also nonsense: rebimboca da parafuseta. It's a made up piece for a machine, used to say a mechanical problem is actually ridiculous or made up, or sometimes as a comic placeholder for any undefined piece of machinery.<br /> <br /> And whenever you see a term in English that's actually Latim or French, it's probably actually universal, especially if it is deliberately spelled in the original language. But Shanghaiing was new to me, indeed.<br /> <br /> But hey, here we took your &quot;delete&quot; and created &quot;deletar&quot; (verb), &quot;deletado&quot; (adj), and did the same to &quot;start&quot; and several others. Mouse in Brazilian Portuguese is &quot;camundongo&quot;, but the computer input is &quot;mouse&quot; with a more open &quot;o&quot;.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}